1
00:00:25,826 --> 00:00:28,125
♪♪

2
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,305
♪♪

3
00:00:49,349 --> 00:00:51,341
♪♪

4
00:01:17,311 --> 00:01:19,303
♪♪

5
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:49,132
♪♪

6
00:02:17,571 --> 00:02:19,563
♪♪

7
00:02:48,735 --> 00:02:50,146
It's all here.

8
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:51,447
Everything you wanted,

9
00:02:51,471 --> 00:02:54,617
from automatic weapons
to Redeye missiles.

10
00:02:54,641 --> 00:02:56,386
Usual mint condition.

11
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:58,388
Now, this really
going to be it for you?

12
00:02:58,412 --> 00:02:59,722
No more orders?

13
00:02:59,746 --> 00:03:00,890
This is it.

14
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:02,314
Where's the rig?

15
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,794
I didn't bring it.

16
00:03:04,818 --> 00:03:06,596
How'd you get out here?

17
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,698
- I jogged.
- No kidding?

18
00:03:08,722 --> 00:03:10,156
How you going to get back?

19
00:04:03,143 --> 00:04:05,254
I don't feel
comfortable about this.

20
00:04:05,278 --> 00:04:06,723
I don't like putting somebody

21
00:04:06,747 --> 00:04:08,691
on the stand I
haven't talked to.

22
00:04:08,715 --> 00:04:10,259
She only got in this morning,

23
00:04:10,283 --> 00:04:12,184
and she's leaving
this afternoon.

24
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:20,369
So, uh... um...

25
00:04:20,393 --> 00:04:22,605
Ms. Anderson...
Mrs. Anderson? Yeah.

26
00:04:22,629 --> 00:04:25,541
Uh, would you tell
us where you were

27
00:04:25,565 --> 00:04:31,247
at approximately 1:30 on
the afternoon of September 2?

28
00:04:31,271 --> 00:04:34,383
Uh-huh. I was at the parking lot

29
00:04:34,407 --> 00:04:38,154
at the Westlake branch of
Monument Savings and Loan.

30
00:04:38,178 --> 00:04:41,057
Uh-huh. And what did you
see while you were there?

31
00:04:41,081 --> 00:04:44,026
Yeah, I saw a man come
running out of the bank

32
00:04:44,050 --> 00:04:46,429
who was carrying a
briefcase in one hand

33
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:49,665
and pulling off a wig and
sunglasses with the other.

34
00:04:49,689 --> 00:04:51,400
He-he just stuffed
everything in his briefcase,

35
00:04:51,424 --> 00:04:52,769
and he kept right on running.

36
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,403
Huh. Uh, uh, would...

37
00:04:54,427 --> 00:04:56,539
He had long, wavy blond hair

38
00:04:56,563 --> 00:04:58,862
and thick lips.

39
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,644
Thick lips?

40
00:05:01,668 --> 00:05:02,678
Yeah, real thick.

41
00:05:02,702 --> 00:05:03,780
See, that's not the guy.

42
00:05:03,804 --> 00:05:05,796
See how thin his lips are?

43
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,221
Yeah, he does have
moderately thin lips.

44
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:13,923
- Doesn't he?
- Yeah.

45
00:05:13,947 --> 00:05:18,027
Ordinarily, I don't notice
the lip size on a man.

46
00:05:18,051 --> 00:05:20,530
I guess that's
because I'm a man.

47
00:05:20,554 --> 00:05:22,098
Sure. I mean, that...

48
00:05:22,122 --> 00:05:23,399
that certainly makes sense.

49
00:05:23,423 --> 00:05:25,434
But see, I'm a girl,

50
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:28,471
and lip size is one
of the very first things

51
00:05:28,495 --> 00:05:31,107
that I notice, especially
when they're thick.

52
00:05:31,131 --> 00:05:32,608
- Uh-huh. Good.
- Isn't it?

53
00:05:32,632 --> 00:05:35,611
Yeah, I mean, he is not the guy.

54
00:05:35,635 --> 00:05:37,413
I don't even know
why he's on trial,

55
00:05:37,437 --> 00:05:40,583
because the real bank robber
has blond hair and thick lips.

56
00:05:40,607 --> 00:05:42,652
- Thick lips.
- Very thick.

57
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:46,322
And that man over there
has dark hair and very thin lips.

58
00:05:46,346 --> 00:05:48,906
Thin lips.

59
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:53,663
Uh, Your Honor, might I
have a word with my client?

60
00:05:53,687 --> 00:05:55,656
Go ahead, Mr. Matlock.

61
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:09,879
You're dead.

62
00:06:09,903 --> 00:06:11,247
What?

63
00:06:11,271 --> 00:06:12,882
You know this girl,

64
00:06:12,906 --> 00:06:15,585
and you put her up
to this, Mr. Thin Lips.

65
00:06:15,609 --> 00:06:16,853
I wouldn't do that to her.

66
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:17,920
She's a friend of mine.

67
00:06:17,944 --> 00:06:20,723
She... she volunteered.

68
00:06:20,747 --> 00:06:21,991
You're dead.

69
00:06:22,015 --> 00:06:23,659
- No further questions.
- But...

70
00:06:23,683 --> 00:06:25,194
You're dead.

71
00:06:25,218 --> 00:06:27,530
Your witness.

72
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,546
Thank you, Your Honor.

73
00:06:32,459 --> 00:06:35,872
This man whom you
saw run from the bank...

74
00:06:35,896 --> 00:06:38,127
What color raincoat
was he wearing?

75
00:06:39,766 --> 00:06:43,012
Um... gray?

76
00:06:43,036 --> 00:06:44,380
Well, the bank teller

77
00:06:44,404 --> 00:06:48,136
whom he robbed at gunpoint
testified it was navy blue.

78
00:06:49,609 --> 00:06:51,921
Well, maybe it was reversible.

79
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:57,260
You're dead, and
I hate you for it.

80
00:07:04,391 --> 00:07:06,383
Mrs. Hawkins.

81
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:09,405
Mrs. Hawkins!

82
00:07:09,429 --> 00:07:11,307
You lost your case, didn't you?

83
00:07:11,331 --> 00:07:13,309
- Mrs. Hawkins...
- I knew you were going

84
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:14,577
- to lose that case.
- Mrs. Hawkins...

85
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:15,878
I didn't want to say anything,

86
00:07:15,902 --> 00:07:18,381
but, uh, I knew
from your horoscope.

87
00:07:18,405 --> 00:07:20,917
- Mrs. Hawkins...
- If you'd just ask.

88
00:07:20,941 --> 00:07:24,387
Now you got a bad mark
against you with the courthouse.

89
00:07:24,411 --> 00:07:27,223
Mrs. Hawkins, never
mind about that now.

90
00:07:27,247 --> 00:07:29,959
Now, when you... when
you came to work for me,

91
00:07:29,983 --> 00:07:34,230
I made a... a big deal about not
messing with stuff on my desk.

92
00:07:34,254 --> 00:07:35,765
I can't find anything.

93
00:07:35,789 --> 00:07:37,600
Mr. Matlock, your
desk was a sight.

94
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,802
All I did was put
things in order.

95
00:07:39,826 --> 00:07:41,137
I don't want things in order.

96
00:07:41,161 --> 00:07:43,139
I want them left
just as they are.

97
00:07:43,163 --> 00:07:45,174
I was working on
a brief last night.

98
00:07:45,198 --> 00:07:46,909
Had "Hartsell and Pruitt" on it.

99
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:48,697
Now it's gone.

100
00:07:53,273 --> 00:07:55,251
Well, how was I to know?

101
00:07:55,275 --> 00:07:58,955
Mr. Matlock, I worked
this way for 15 years

102
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:01,624
for Mr. Gaskins,
God rest his soul,

103
00:08:01,648 --> 00:08:03,259
and he never once complained.

104
00:08:03,283 --> 00:08:05,161
And I did everything for him...

105
00:08:05,185 --> 00:08:08,464
Planning, arranging...
Right up to the end.

106
00:08:08,488 --> 00:08:11,253
I even chose the
suit he was laid out in.

107
00:08:12,759 --> 00:08:15,338
Well, that won't be
such a problem here.

108
00:08:15,362 --> 00:08:19,175
See, I only wear this one
type of suit, and this is it.

109
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:21,911
All you got to do
is choose the one

110
00:08:21,935 --> 00:08:23,479
that just came back
from the cleaners.

111
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:26,473
Or not. It won't make
much difference then.

112
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:30,186
A dark shade is
more appropriate.

113
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:32,975
I'm not buying a dark
suit for that one occasion.

114
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:35,291
You could always rent.

115
00:08:35,315 --> 00:08:37,493
If I rent,

116
00:08:37,517 --> 00:08:40,529
I guess they take it off
me right after the service

117
00:08:40,553 --> 00:08:42,565
and stick me in
the ground naked.

118
00:08:42,589 --> 00:08:45,735
I don't want to go
see Mr. Jesus naked.

119
00:08:45,759 --> 00:08:46,969
Ben.

120
00:08:46,993 --> 00:08:48,804
What?

121
00:08:48,828 --> 00:08:50,888
You want to open the door?

122
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,645
Hi, Mrs. Hawkins.

123
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:58,381
- Hello.
- Ben.

124
00:08:58,405 --> 00:08:59,815
Well, I said, "What?"

125
00:08:59,839 --> 00:09:00,950
Plane tickets.

126
00:09:00,974 --> 00:09:02,051
To where?

127
00:09:02,075 --> 00:09:03,586
Remember? You
promised the publisher

128
00:09:03,610 --> 00:09:05,421
of the <i>Los Angeles
Chronicle</i> that you'd defend

129
00:09:05,445 --> 00:09:07,641
one of his reporters when
his contempt trial came up.

130
00:09:09,682 --> 00:09:13,662
But I just lost a case and
I'm starting another one.

131
00:09:13,686 --> 00:09:14,663
I'll get a continuance.

132
00:09:14,687 --> 00:09:17,333
The contempt trial
starts tomorrow.

133
00:09:17,357 --> 00:09:20,850
Well, I guess I did promise.

134
00:09:21,895 --> 00:09:25,107
Oh, I guess I'd better go pack.

135
00:09:25,131 --> 00:09:27,109
How important is this case?

136
00:09:27,133 --> 00:09:28,644
- What?
- Don't go.

137
00:09:28,668 --> 00:09:29,678
What are you talking about?

138
00:09:29,702 --> 00:09:30,679
You're Gemini.

139
00:09:30,703 --> 00:09:31,680
Don't go.

140
00:09:31,704 --> 00:09:33,015
Mrs. Hawkins...

141
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:34,650
All right, don't listen to me,

142
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:36,152
but here's your
horoscope for today,

143
00:09:36,176 --> 00:09:40,739
and remember, this day started
with you already losing a case.

144
00:09:45,718 --> 00:09:48,964
"Your lunar aspect does
not coincide with travel.

145
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:50,833
"Business call suggests trip.

146
00:09:50,857 --> 00:09:52,268
"Hold off.

147
00:09:52,292 --> 00:09:56,605
"Be diplomatic and interested,
but avoid becoming involved.

148
00:09:56,629 --> 00:09:58,474
"Entertain at home tonight.

149
00:09:58,498 --> 00:10:00,509
"You'll be complimented
on appearance.

150
00:10:00,533 --> 00:10:03,059
Feature colors."

151
00:10:04,037 --> 00:10:06,063
I'll go pack.

152
00:10:08,108 --> 00:10:10,686
Can't you stop him?

153
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:11,987
What's your sign?

154
00:10:12,011 --> 00:10:13,856
Um... Aquarius?

155
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:14,924
Oh, that's perfect.

156
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,659
You're compatible with Gemini.

157
00:10:16,683 --> 00:10:17,993
- Talk to him.
- Mrs. Hawkins,

158
00:10:18,017 --> 00:10:20,496
- I really don't think...
- You know what Geminis are like.

159
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,497
They're dependent on others.

160
00:10:21,521 --> 00:10:23,232
They need us.

161
00:10:23,256 --> 00:10:24,266
They're always calling for help.

162
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,290
Help!

163
00:10:28,328 --> 00:10:30,661
Where are my shirts?

164
00:10:35,335 --> 00:10:36,912
Your attention, please...

165
00:10:36,936 --> 00:10:38,647
You canceled my flight?

166
00:10:38,671 --> 00:10:40,249
Equipment problems.

167
00:10:40,273 --> 00:10:42,651
I'm booking you on Flight 532.

168
00:10:42,675 --> 00:10:44,353
Departs at 9:45 from Gate 3C.

169
00:10:44,377 --> 00:10:47,857
That's three hours from now.

170
00:10:47,881 --> 00:10:49,725
I'm not waiting around
here three hours.

171
00:10:49,749 --> 00:10:51,360
I'll use another airline.

172
00:10:51,384 --> 00:10:54,830
This is our super bonanza
weekend discount fare.

173
00:10:54,854 --> 00:10:56,765
No other airline
can come close to it.

174
00:10:56,789 --> 00:10:59,768
You mean it'll cost me
more to use another airline?

175
00:10:59,792 --> 00:11:02,138
Much more.

176
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:04,673
Dallas, St. Louis
or San Francisco,

177
00:11:04,697 --> 00:11:06,928
please contact the airline...

178
00:11:10,904 --> 00:11:12,214
Excuse me, please.

179
00:11:12,238 --> 00:11:13,349
That can't be right.

180
00:11:13,373 --> 00:11:14,850
I'm supposed to be
in business class.

181
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:17,086
Please sit down, sir,
you're blocking the aisle.

182
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:20,956
Oh, well... Ma'am.

183
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:24,007
You couldn't get here
five minutes earlier?

184
00:11:37,597 --> 00:11:39,909
Excuse me.

185
00:12:32,719 --> 00:12:34,263
What's the count?

186
00:12:34,287 --> 00:12:35,464
All right. Thanks.

187
00:12:35,488 --> 00:12:36,632
You lost my bag.

188
00:12:36,656 --> 00:12:37,800
Fill this out, please.

189
00:12:37,824 --> 00:12:39,235
How could you lose my bag?

190
00:12:39,259 --> 00:12:41,604
You had three hours
to put it on the airplane.

191
00:12:41,628 --> 00:12:43,872
If we don't get your bag
to you within 24 hours,

192
00:12:43,896 --> 00:12:45,808
you'll receive a
free round-trip ticket

193
00:12:45,832 --> 00:12:47,243
to any city we fly to.

194
00:12:47,267 --> 00:12:50,760
Now... which suitcase
looks like yours?

195
00:12:52,972 --> 00:12:55,317
Welcome to Los Angeles
International Airport.

196
00:12:55,341 --> 00:12:57,810
Shuttle buses available
for the downtown area...

197
00:13:04,050 --> 00:13:06,362
<i>I know, Mrs. Hawkins.</i>

198
00:13:06,386 --> 00:13:07,796
I know.

199
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,298
Well, I warned you, didn't I?

200
00:13:09,322 --> 00:13:10,666
Didn't your horoscope tell you?

201
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:12,635
You're lucky you
only lost your luggage.

202
00:13:12,659 --> 00:13:14,136
You could have
crashed, you could have...

203
00:13:14,160 --> 00:13:17,239
Well, I'm here now,
but I need some clothes.

204
00:13:17,263 --> 00:13:20,376
Send a suit and-and some
shirts, and s... and underwear

205
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:21,577
and socks.

206
00:13:21,601 --> 00:13:23,379
And whatever else you do today,

207
00:13:23,403 --> 00:13:26,682
for heaven's sake, avoid
contact with a Capricorn.

208
00:13:26,706 --> 00:13:28,717
Stay away from Capricorn.

209
00:13:28,741 --> 00:13:30,319
Right. No Capricorns.

210
00:13:30,343 --> 00:13:32,988
And I don't care what
else I have to focus on.

211
00:13:33,012 --> 00:13:34,990
Just send the clothes.

212
00:13:38,951 --> 00:13:40,162
Okay, I'm ready.

213
00:13:40,186 --> 00:13:42,064
Well, Mr. Matlock...
It is Matlock, isn't it?

214
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:43,232
Yeah, yeah.

215
00:13:43,256 --> 00:13:45,234
Mr. Matlock, I'm sorry.

216
00:13:45,258 --> 00:13:47,202
It seems that we have...

217
00:13:47,226 --> 00:13:49,738
You gave my room away?

218
00:13:49,762 --> 00:13:51,840
Well, since you neither arrived,

219
00:13:51,864 --> 00:13:53,742
nor called by 10:00
p.m. last night,

220
00:13:53,766 --> 00:13:55,244
we gave your room
to somebody else.

221
00:13:55,268 --> 00:13:59,448
At 10:00 p.m. last night, I
was 40,000 feet in the air.

222
00:13:59,472 --> 00:14:01,583
I'm due in court in two hours.

223
00:14:01,607 --> 00:14:05,220
I need to shave, shower,
and I want my room!

224
00:14:05,244 --> 00:14:06,388
Please, sir, lower your voice.

225
00:14:06,412 --> 00:14:09,358
Not until I get my room!

226
00:14:09,382 --> 00:14:11,226
Have a good one.

227
00:14:11,250 --> 00:14:13,276
Yeah, you, too, Buehler.

228
00:14:21,828 --> 00:14:23,305
Oh.

229
00:14:23,329 --> 00:14:25,841
Oh. Have you got
a styptic pencil?

230
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,209
Huh?

231
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:29,778
You know those white things
for when you cut yourself?

232
00:14:29,802 --> 00:14:31,780
<i>Perdón, Señor, no
entiendo Io que dice,</i>

233
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:33,482
<i>y no tengo tiempo
contestar las preguntas,</i>

234
00:14:33,506 --> 00:14:35,017
<i>porque tengo que trabajar.</i>

235
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:07,816
I realize this is highly
irregular, Your Honor.

236
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:10,285
I have been acting as
counsel to Mr. Thorndike

237
00:15:10,309 --> 00:15:12,287
on a temporary basis only,

238
00:15:12,311 --> 00:15:14,656
and since the man who
was to represent him

239
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:17,960
in this matter seems, at
the moment, to be missing...

240
00:15:17,984 --> 00:15:19,128
Ben Matlock for the defense.

241
00:15:19,152 --> 00:15:20,295
I'm sorry I'm late, Your Honor.

242
00:15:20,319 --> 00:15:21,897
Got here as soon as I could.

243
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:23,599
Mr. Matlock, if
you're quite ready,

244
00:15:23,623 --> 00:15:25,200
let's get started.

245
00:15:25,224 --> 00:15:28,103
Uh, may I have a brief
recess to confer with my client?

246
00:15:28,127 --> 00:15:29,271
No.

247
00:15:29,295 --> 00:15:30,906
An hour at the most, maybe two?

248
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:33,942
Mr. Matlock, this case has
been continued four times.

249
00:15:33,966 --> 00:15:37,146
I frankly am sick and tired
of seeing it on my calendar.

250
00:15:37,170 --> 00:15:39,014
I will tolerate no more delays.

251
00:15:39,038 --> 00:15:40,315
But, Your Honor...

252
00:15:40,339 --> 00:15:41,917
The defendant, William
Thorndike, is charged

253
00:15:41,941 --> 00:15:43,185
with three separate counts

254
00:15:43,209 --> 00:15:45,854
of willfully refusing
to answer questions

255
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:47,222
after this court's denial

256
00:15:47,246 --> 00:15:49,291
of his claim of immunity
from disclosure.

257
00:15:49,315 --> 00:15:50,292
Your Honor, please.

258
00:15:50,316 --> 00:15:53,395
Mr. Matlock, I
understand that in Atlanta

259
00:15:53,419 --> 00:15:55,264
you have something
of a celebrity status,

260
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:56,799
but I want to assure you

261
00:15:56,823 --> 00:15:59,101
that that will get you
nowhere in my courtroom.

262
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:01,670
Now, I don't want to hear
another word out of you

263
00:16:01,694 --> 00:16:04,540
until the prosecution has
presented its arguments.

264
00:16:04,564 --> 00:16:07,466
Is that perfectly clear?

265
00:16:09,402 --> 00:16:11,380
Yes, sir.

266
00:16:11,404 --> 00:16:14,183
Mr. Shepard, you may begin.

267
00:16:16,576 --> 00:16:19,321
No, sir, I can't
do it. It's not right.

268
00:16:19,345 --> 00:16:20,689
Mr. Matlock.

269
00:16:20,713 --> 00:16:22,691
I can't let you
penalize my client...

270
00:16:22,715 --> 00:16:23,959
Mr. Matlock, sit down.

271
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:26,061
Just because my plane
was late, I lost my luggage,

272
00:16:26,085 --> 00:16:28,330
- and my room got all screwed up.
- Sit down and be quiet

273
00:16:28,354 --> 00:16:29,765
or I will find you in contempt.

274
00:16:29,789 --> 00:16:30,999
My client has a
constitutional right

275
00:16:31,023 --> 00:16:32,201
to adequate
counsel, and right now

276
00:16:32,225 --> 00:16:34,303
- there's no way in
hell - Mr. Matlock?

277
00:16:34,327 --> 00:16:36,038
The word "adequate"
can be applied to me.

278
00:16:36,062 --> 00:16:37,473
- You are in contempt.
- Huh?

279
00:16:37,497 --> 00:16:40,008
Bailiff, you are instructed
to take Mr. Matlock

280
00:16:40,032 --> 00:16:41,343
into immediate custody
and place him in lockup

281
00:16:41,367 --> 00:16:43,312
until such time as a hearing

282
00:16:43,336 --> 00:16:44,980
on his own contempt
charges may be set.

283
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:47,516
What am I supposed
to give to my client...?!

284
00:16:54,747 --> 00:16:57,459
Man, don't know
nothing, you know?

285
00:17:08,561 --> 00:17:10,839
What's your sign?

286
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,074
Huh?

287
00:17:12,098 --> 00:17:14,276
Your sign. You know,
astrology, your horoscope.

288
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:16,245
Oh, that. Capricorn.

289
00:17:16,269 --> 00:17:18,261
Hmm.

290
00:17:22,675 --> 00:17:24,667
Mr. Matlock?

291
00:17:26,012 --> 00:17:27,222
Hearing's over.

292
00:17:27,246 --> 00:17:28,590
Judge Price rescinded his order.

293
00:17:28,614 --> 00:17:29,758
Oh.

294
00:17:29,782 --> 00:17:32,027
Guess he just wanted
to teach you a lesson.

295
00:17:32,051 --> 00:17:34,496
Well, what happened after
they threw me out of there?

296
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,265
Well, Judge Price granted
another continuance.

297
00:17:36,289 --> 00:17:37,799
When's the next hearing?

298
00:17:37,823 --> 00:17:40,168
Well, he said he wasn't going
to put it back on his calendar

299
00:17:40,192 --> 00:17:42,137
until he was, quote,
"damned good and ready."

300
00:17:42,161 --> 00:17:44,907
It's an outrage to my client.

301
00:17:44,931 --> 00:17:47,175
Oh, well, I really don't
think he much cares.

302
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:48,911
Oh.

303
00:17:48,935 --> 00:17:51,079
So, what are you gonna do now?

304
00:17:51,103 --> 00:17:53,849
Well, one thing
I'm <i>not</i> gonna do...

305
00:17:53,873 --> 00:17:57,219
I'm not making
another trip out here.

306
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:59,221
Mr. Matlock, if you're
thinking of going to see him,

307
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:01,189
there's something I
ought to tell you first.

308
00:18:01,213 --> 00:18:02,991
What?

309
00:18:03,015 --> 00:18:05,694
You've got toilet
paper on your face.

310
00:18:05,718 --> 00:18:07,914
Oh.

311
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:14,903
Mm-hmm.

312
00:18:16,696 --> 00:18:18,373
Uh, you can't beat that.

313
00:18:19,632 --> 00:18:20,809
We're wasting time here.

314
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:22,077
We got to talk.

315
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:23,879
Discussion's closed.

316
00:18:23,903 --> 00:18:25,547
Raymond's right, Daryl.

317
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:28,383
He's stated his position,
he's not gonna budge.

318
00:18:28,407 --> 00:18:30,319
Further talk is pointless.

319
00:18:30,343 --> 00:18:32,087
What about you?

320
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:34,089
You're just gonna
roll over, too?

321
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,091
I think Raymond is wrong.

322
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:38,260
I think I <i>can</i> beat that.

323
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:39,877
Hey, Judge Price?!

324
00:18:40,987 --> 00:18:42,979
Hey.

325
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:46,068
Your Honor, we've got to talk.

326
00:18:46,092 --> 00:18:47,836
You're interrupting our game.

327
00:18:47,860 --> 00:18:49,004
I can see that.

328
00:18:49,028 --> 00:18:51,206
How would you
like to go back to jail

329
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:52,708
on a harassment
charge this time?

330
00:18:52,732 --> 00:18:54,710
Judge Price, the
Constitution says

331
00:18:54,734 --> 00:18:57,746
that my client has the
right to a speedy trial.

332
00:18:57,770 --> 00:18:59,314
You cannot, and I will not

333
00:18:59,338 --> 00:19:01,149
discuss your client's
case at this time.

334
00:19:01,173 --> 00:19:04,119
This has nothing to do with
my client, and you know it.

335
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:05,721
You're madder than hell at me.

336
00:19:05,745 --> 00:19:07,155
Now, you <i>will</i> hear this case,

337
00:19:07,179 --> 00:19:09,658
or I <i>will</i> file a complaint.

338
00:19:09,682 --> 00:19:11,674
You're asking for trouble.

339
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:17,032
Trouble is a two-way
street, Your Honor.

340
00:19:17,056 --> 00:19:20,035
Are you threatening
me, Mr. Matlock?

341
00:19:20,059 --> 00:19:22,153
I'm trying to do my job.

342
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:26,942
My chambers, 7:00 tonight.

343
00:19:26,966 --> 00:19:28,377
Settle it now.

344
00:19:28,401 --> 00:19:30,379
My chambers, 7:00 tonight!

345
00:19:30,403 --> 00:19:33,805
All right. Your chambers, 7:00.

346
00:19:54,827 --> 00:19:57,058
What the hell are
you doing here?

347
00:19:59,832 --> 00:20:02,631
Just wanted to talk.

348
00:20:03,669 --> 00:20:06,948
I've made up my mind, Walker.

349
00:20:06,972 --> 00:20:09,618
Yeah.

350
00:20:09,642 --> 00:20:11,720
I know.

351
00:20:11,744 --> 00:20:13,076
Too bad.

352
00:20:18,517 --> 00:20:21,963
Uh, excuse me, I'm
here to see Judge Price.

353
00:20:21,987 --> 00:20:23,699
Yes, he came in
about ten minutes ago.

354
00:20:23,723 --> 00:20:25,434
- Okay.
- Fourth floor.

355
00:20:25,458 --> 00:20:27,689
Fourth floor.

356
00:20:31,130 --> 00:20:33,122
Right through there.

357
00:20:57,389 --> 00:20:59,381
Judge Price?

358
00:21:29,722 --> 00:21:31,714
♪♪

359
00:21:59,185 --> 00:22:02,678
♪♪

360
00:22:28,948 --> 00:22:30,940
Yeah.

361
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:35,011
A drink.

362
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,183
What'll it be?

363
00:22:39,225 --> 00:22:43,361
Uh... one like that.

364
00:22:45,798 --> 00:22:48,734
Coming right up.

365
00:22:52,938 --> 00:22:55,717
Hey, hey, did...

366
00:22:55,741 --> 00:23:01,790
did you-did you-did you
know Judge Raymond Price?

367
00:23:01,814 --> 00:23:03,725
A personal friend of mine.

368
00:23:03,749 --> 00:23:06,194
Yeah?

369
00:23:06,218 --> 00:23:07,662
He's dead.

370
00:23:07,686 --> 00:23:09,798
Yeah, yeah.

371
00:23:09,822 --> 00:23:15,036
He-he was... he
was... he was a jackass,

372
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:18,006
a real jackass, but he...

373
00:23:18,030 --> 00:23:20,966
he didn't deserve to be dead.

374
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:30,485
Mmm.

375
00:23:30,509 --> 00:23:32,120
That'll be $2.50.

376
00:23:32,144 --> 00:23:34,623
Okay.

377
00:23:41,787 --> 00:23:45,033
I guess I'll have to
open an account.

378
00:23:46,358 --> 00:23:47,553
Guess again.

379
00:24:17,389 --> 00:24:19,722
♪♪

380
00:24:26,365 --> 00:24:28,209
Where... where's your money?

381
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:29,511
I don't know.

382
00:24:29,535 --> 00:24:32,732
Don't-don't take my...
Don't take my watch!

383
00:25:17,850 --> 00:25:20,895
Mr. Matlock.

384
00:25:20,919 --> 00:25:22,945
Lieutenant Judd Myerson.

385
00:25:24,590 --> 00:25:27,969
As you know, you have
the right to remain silent.

386
00:25:27,993 --> 00:25:31,406
Anything you say, can
and will be used against you.

387
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:34,209
You can forget all that part.

388
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:37,078
What's on your mind?

389
00:25:37,102 --> 00:25:39,333
Let's talk about last night.

390
00:25:41,507 --> 00:25:43,752
I don't remember last night.

391
00:25:43,776 --> 00:25:47,922
At about 11:30, you
entered Angels Tavern.

392
00:25:47,946 --> 00:25:49,524
You ordered a drink.

393
00:25:49,548 --> 00:25:52,727
You asked the bartender if he
knew Judge Raymond T. Price.

394
00:25:52,751 --> 00:25:55,764
Then you told him
the judge was dead.

395
00:25:55,788 --> 00:25:58,666
And then you
called him a jackass.

396
00:25:58,690 --> 00:26:00,735
I did?

397
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:03,471
You went to see the
judge about 7:00 last night.

398
00:26:03,495 --> 00:26:05,327
Do you remember that?

399
00:26:09,201 --> 00:26:10,965
Yeah.

400
00:26:12,004 --> 00:26:14,282
Yeah. He was lying on the floor.

401
00:26:14,306 --> 00:26:16,117
He looked like he was dead.

402
00:26:16,141 --> 00:26:18,787
He was dead all right.

403
00:26:18,811 --> 00:26:20,109
He was murdered.

404
00:26:21,146 --> 00:26:22,624
Do you know who did it?

405
00:26:22,648 --> 00:26:24,559
Do you?

406
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:28,129
Let's see, I...

407
00:26:28,153 --> 00:26:32,801
I saw the judge
lying on the floor.

408
00:26:32,825 --> 00:26:36,604
And then... somebody...

409
00:26:36,628 --> 00:26:39,274
somebody hit me and choked me.

410
00:26:39,298 --> 00:26:41,631
I-I must have blacked out.

411
00:26:44,503 --> 00:26:46,548
Wait a minute,

412
00:26:46,572 --> 00:26:50,518
I saw somebody in the
mirror, just before he hit me.

413
00:26:50,542 --> 00:26:51,986
Must have been the murderer.

414
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:54,823
Where-where are your mug books?

415
00:26:54,847 --> 00:26:57,225
If I can see his picture,
I might recognize him.

416
00:26:57,249 --> 00:26:59,327
That won't be necessary.

417
00:26:59,351 --> 00:27:01,445
I want to see those
books right now.

418
00:27:03,489 --> 00:27:05,366
According to passport records,

419
00:27:05,390 --> 00:27:07,969
the only fingerprints on the
murder weapon are yours.

420
00:27:07,993 --> 00:27:10,638
You had a loud disagreement

421
00:27:10,662 --> 00:27:12,507
with the judge in
court yesterday.

422
00:27:12,531 --> 00:27:14,709
You were seen entering the
courthouse less than an hour

423
00:27:14,733 --> 00:27:16,725
before the body was discovered.

424
00:27:19,071 --> 00:27:22,083
And you told the
bartender at Angels Tavern

425
00:27:22,107 --> 00:27:23,985
that the judge was dead.

426
00:27:24,009 --> 00:27:27,021
It may be hard to
believe, Mr. Matlock,

427
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:30,058
but that makes you
our prime suspect.

428
00:27:30,082 --> 00:27:34,062
You've got to be kidding.

429
00:27:34,086 --> 00:27:37,181
The D.A. isn't.

430
00:28:07,019 --> 00:28:10,012
♪♪

431
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:19,388
All right, come on,
keep it moving, guys.

432
00:28:20,933 --> 00:28:24,279
Ben, Ben.

433
00:28:24,303 --> 00:28:25,980
I can't believe this.

434
00:28:26,004 --> 00:28:27,582
Are you all right?

435
00:28:27,606 --> 00:28:30,218
- Yeah.
- We're gonna get you out of here

436
00:28:30,242 --> 00:28:31,286
as soon as we can.

437
00:28:31,310 --> 00:28:32,554
We're fifth on the docket.

438
00:28:32,578 --> 00:28:36,891
Got some clean clothes
for you back at the hotel.

439
00:28:36,915 --> 00:28:40,528
Oh. I'm glad you're here.

440
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:42,851
Come on, keep it moving.

441
00:28:45,390 --> 00:28:46,901
The defendant's
not from this city

442
00:28:46,925 --> 00:28:49,204
or even this state,
Your Honor, and to say

443
00:28:49,228 --> 00:28:50,905
that he has no ties
to this community

444
00:28:50,929 --> 00:28:52,240
is a gross understatement.

445
00:28:52,264 --> 00:28:54,309
Hey, I've been a member
of the Bar in good standing

446
00:28:54,333 --> 00:28:56,611
since before you knew
what the word "gross" meant!

447
00:28:56,635 --> 00:28:58,947
Uh, Your Honor, my client,

448
00:28:58,971 --> 00:29:01,182
as you may know, or by
now may have guessed,

449
00:29:01,206 --> 00:29:02,483
is an attorney.

450
00:29:02,507 --> 00:29:04,786
He's, uh, a member
of the Bar in five states.

451
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:06,187
His record and reputation

452
00:29:06,211 --> 00:29:09,991
as an officer of the court in
all of them is unblemished.

453
00:29:10,015 --> 00:29:11,159
It's absurd to
think that there's

454
00:29:11,183 --> 00:29:12,560
any risk of flight here at all.

455
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:14,429
In fact, I recommend
that he be released

456
00:29:14,453 --> 00:29:16,664
on his own recognizance.

457
00:29:16,688 --> 00:29:18,666
My main concern here
is not the risk of flight.

458
00:29:18,690 --> 00:29:20,368
This was a particularly
heinous crime.

459
00:29:20,392 --> 00:29:24,172
A jurist was murdered...
A fellow jurist.

460
00:29:24,196 --> 00:29:26,007
Bail is set at $250,000.

461
00:29:26,031 --> 00:29:27,575
Next case.

462
00:29:27,599 --> 00:29:28,910
$250,000?!

463
00:29:28,934 --> 00:29:30,245
That's a quarter of a million!

464
00:29:30,269 --> 00:29:31,813
- It's okay, Ben.
- It's not okay!

465
00:29:31,837 --> 00:29:33,047
I'm not John Dillinger!

466
00:29:33,071 --> 00:29:36,451
- $250,000.
- 250... Highway robbery!

467
00:29:36,475 --> 00:29:37,852
You're John Dillinger!

468
00:29:37,876 --> 00:29:38,987
Next case.

469
00:29:49,421 --> 00:29:51,754
Empty 'em.

470
00:30:27,559 --> 00:30:29,270
Hey!

471
00:30:29,294 --> 00:30:31,172
You stole my watch!

472
00:30:31,196 --> 00:30:32,774
- Oh, I-I-I'm sorry.
- Yeah? Yeah? Yeah?

473
00:30:32,798 --> 00:30:35,043
You-you can have
it back. It's yours.

474
00:30:35,067 --> 00:30:36,210
It's his!

475
00:30:36,234 --> 00:30:38,346
See, I...

476
00:30:38,370 --> 00:30:39,747
I didn't even... I
didn't even hock it.

477
00:30:39,771 --> 00:30:41,149
I didn't have time to hock it.

478
00:30:41,173 --> 00:30:43,451
See? It's a good thing that
I mugged you when I did.

479
00:30:43,475 --> 00:30:44,852
No.

480
00:30:44,876 --> 00:30:46,621
The way you were staggering
all over that neighborhood,

481
00:30:46,645 --> 00:30:48,637
- you could have got killed.
- Yeah.

482
00:30:57,989 --> 00:30:59,334
You were following me?

483
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:03,237
Uh, yeah, well, you
know, kind of casing you.

484
00:31:03,261 --> 00:31:06,040
I picked you up right outside
of that there warehouse.

485
00:31:06,064 --> 00:31:07,342
What warehouse?!

486
00:31:07,366 --> 00:31:09,711
Uh, the one that you
went into with that guy.

487
00:31:09,735 --> 00:31:10,878
What guy?!

488
00:31:10,902 --> 00:31:12,213
Your buddy.

489
00:31:12,237 --> 00:31:14,349
The guy who practically
dragged you in.

490
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:16,342
What did he look like?

491
00:31:17,943 --> 00:31:19,087
What did he look like?!

492
00:31:19,111 --> 00:31:21,389
Dark-dark hair,
brown-brown, big build.

493
00:31:21,413 --> 00:31:22,757
Big.

494
00:31:22,781 --> 00:31:23,991
Ben.

495
00:31:24,015 --> 00:31:26,461
Bail's been posted.

496
00:31:26,485 --> 00:31:27,862
Good.

497
00:31:27,886 --> 00:31:29,864
Now let's see if you can
get bail for my friend here.

498
00:31:29,888 --> 00:31:31,199
What's your name?

499
00:31:31,223 --> 00:31:33,601
Sloan, Andrew Nathaniel
Ridgeway Sloan.

500
00:31:33,625 --> 00:31:34,820
- Sloan.
- Sloan.

501
00:31:45,370 --> 00:31:47,148
Hi, Conrad. When
did you get here?

502
00:31:47,172 --> 00:31:48,282
As soon as I could.

503
00:31:48,306 --> 00:31:49,684
- You okay?
- Yeah. Yeah.

504
00:31:49,708 --> 00:31:51,176
Conrad, Andrew Sloan.

505
00:31:54,146 --> 00:31:56,391
This is a suite.

506
00:31:56,415 --> 00:31:57,892
It's all they had.

507
00:31:57,916 --> 00:31:59,694
Oh.

508
00:31:59,718 --> 00:32:01,596
- This just came.
- Oh.

509
00:32:01,620 --> 00:32:03,664
Airline found it in Anchorage.

510
00:32:03,688 --> 00:32:06,248
Gave you a free
round-trip ticket.

511
00:32:09,227 --> 00:32:10,705
Why don't you take a bath.

512
00:32:10,729 --> 00:32:13,207
Right now, a nice hot
meal sounds better.

513
00:32:13,231 --> 00:32:15,325
Well, here's a
room service menu.

514
00:32:17,235 --> 00:32:20,381
Order anything I like?

515
00:32:20,405 --> 00:32:21,582
Yeah.

516
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:23,785
- Bottle of wine.
- No wine.

517
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:28,189
Ben Matlock.

518
00:32:28,213 --> 00:32:29,524
I'm calling to see

519
00:32:29,548 --> 00:32:32,059
if the clothes I sent
got there all right.

520
00:32:32,083 --> 00:32:33,895
Not yet, Mrs.
Hawkins, but it's okay.

521
00:32:33,919 --> 00:32:35,730
Michelle brought me some.

522
00:32:35,754 --> 00:32:37,732
I'm going to have more
clothes than I need now.

523
00:32:37,756 --> 00:32:39,000
What floor are you on?

524
00:32:39,024 --> 00:32:40,001
What?

525
00:32:40,025 --> 00:32:41,169
I said what floor are you on?

526
00:32:41,193 --> 00:32:43,571
Don't go above the second floor.

527
00:32:43,595 --> 00:32:44,872
Mrs. Hawkins...

528
00:32:44,896 --> 00:32:48,176
Listen to me... The
moon in your sign

529
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:49,577
warns against heights.

530
00:32:49,601 --> 00:32:51,546
Hello?

531
00:32:51,570 --> 00:32:52,680
Hello?

532
00:32:52,704 --> 00:32:54,282
Let me show you something.

533
00:32:54,306 --> 00:32:55,883
Sure wish I had a little wine.

534
00:32:55,907 --> 00:32:57,375
No wine.

535
00:33:00,812 --> 00:33:02,223
Come in.

536
00:33:02,247 --> 00:33:04,648
CI-Close the door.

537
00:33:09,588 --> 00:33:12,400
That's why I was walking
around like a drunken sailor.

538
00:33:12,424 --> 00:33:13,868
Oh, Ben.

539
00:33:13,892 --> 00:33:15,803
You were shot up
with some kind of drug.

540
00:33:15,827 --> 00:33:16,871
Yeah.

541
00:33:16,895 --> 00:33:18,139
Did you get a blood test?

542
00:33:18,163 --> 00:33:20,241
By the time I came
to, it was too late

543
00:33:20,265 --> 00:33:21,476
and I was in jail.

544
00:33:21,500 --> 00:33:24,479
So what does he
have to do with it?

545
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:26,481
I hope he can help
me find the killer.

546
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:28,216
There were only three people

547
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:30,184
who knew I was going to
the judge's office that night...

548
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:32,253
Those three fellas he
was playing golf with.

549
00:33:32,277 --> 00:33:34,922
But it couldn't have been
one of them, 'cause I saw

550
00:33:34,946 --> 00:33:36,390
the killer's face in the mirror.

551
00:33:36,414 --> 00:33:37,925
So the killer had to be hired

552
00:33:37,949 --> 00:33:40,294
by one of them, 'cause like I
say, they were the only ones

553
00:33:40,318 --> 00:33:41,762
who knew I was
going to be there.

554
00:33:41,786 --> 00:33:42,897
Did you get their names?

555
00:33:42,921 --> 00:33:44,532
I have to call Lieutenant
Myerson back.

556
00:33:44,556 --> 00:33:46,801
Better do that.

557
00:33:46,825 --> 00:33:49,070
Uh, Ben, you need to wash.

558
00:33:49,094 --> 00:33:50,289
Oh, yeah.

559
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:58,246
- Hey, Conrad.
- Yeah.

560
00:33:58,270 --> 00:34:03,484
You know those, uh,
airplane tickets I threw away?

561
00:34:03,508 --> 00:34:05,807
Oh, thanks.

562
00:34:07,779 --> 00:34:09,748
- I'll just get this sterilized.
- Yeah.

563
00:34:16,821 --> 00:34:18,466
Oh, I'm sorry.

564
00:34:20,225 --> 00:34:21,969
I didn't mean to startle you.

565
00:34:21,993 --> 00:34:25,406
Although, I wouldn't have
minded if I caught you.

566
00:34:25,430 --> 00:34:27,975
Michelle Thomas.

567
00:34:27,999 --> 00:34:29,544
You're representing the man

568
00:34:29,568 --> 00:34:31,812
accused of murdering
Raymond Price.

569
00:34:31,836 --> 00:34:34,148
Ben Matlock.

570
00:34:34,172 --> 00:34:35,349
That's right.

571
00:34:35,373 --> 00:34:38,085
Well, I-I'm not
complaining, mind you,

572
00:34:38,109 --> 00:34:40,354
but, uh, what brings you here?

573
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:42,256
Well, according to the
Westhaven Country Club,

574
00:34:42,280 --> 00:34:44,859
you played golf with Judge
Price the day he was murdered.

575
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:46,294
It was Friday.

576
00:34:46,318 --> 00:34:48,663
The four of us always
played golf on Friday.

577
00:34:48,687 --> 00:34:51,032
That means you knew

578
00:34:51,056 --> 00:34:53,491
Mr. Matlock was going to be
seeing Judge Price that night.

579
00:34:55,794 --> 00:34:59,697
Michelle, I want you
to take a look at this.

580
00:35:01,433 --> 00:35:04,779
The four of us in Vietnam, 1968.

581
00:35:04,803 --> 00:35:06,380
Green Berets.

582
00:35:06,404 --> 00:35:07,682
Special Forces.

583
00:35:07,706 --> 00:35:10,384
Missions into Cambodia mostly.

584
00:35:10,408 --> 00:35:12,687
We trusted each other,

585
00:35:12,711 --> 00:35:15,256
depended on each other

586
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:17,558
and put our lives on
the line for each other.

587
00:35:17,582 --> 00:35:20,895
Friendships forged
during the heat of battle

588
00:35:20,919 --> 00:35:23,411
last forever, believe me.

589
00:35:25,890 --> 00:35:28,169
Well, thank you, Mr. Prescott.

590
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:31,706
Well, um, do you
have to run off so soon?

591
00:35:31,730 --> 00:35:35,710
Um... gee, my next appointment
isn't for another 20 minutes.

592
00:35:35,734 --> 00:35:38,946
I could give you a lesson.

593
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:41,371
Fly casting?

594
00:35:42,407 --> 00:35:44,376
Whatever.

595
00:36:10,902 --> 00:36:12,179
This is the warehouse.

596
00:36:12,203 --> 00:36:13,714
- This?
- Yeah.

597
00:36:13,738 --> 00:36:17,685
I was sleeping off my wine
under them there boxes.

598
00:36:17,709 --> 00:36:19,787
Hiya, Tierney.

599
00:36:19,811 --> 00:36:24,291
If-if you were asleep, how
could you see anything?

600
00:36:24,315 --> 00:36:25,960
A car door slammed, woke me up.

601
00:36:25,984 --> 00:36:28,696
Thought maybe it was
the cops so I looked out.

602
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:31,999
Saw that brown-haired
guy dragging you inside.

603
00:36:32,023 --> 00:36:34,402
Oh. Oh.

604
00:36:34,426 --> 00:36:37,071
What kind of car was he driving?

605
00:36:37,095 --> 00:36:38,639
Dark.

606
00:36:38,663 --> 00:36:40,975
Uh, not too big.

607
00:36:40,999 --> 00:36:43,594
Not too small.

608
00:37:20,905 --> 00:37:23,340
We must have just
missed somebody.

609
00:38:15,026 --> 00:38:17,338
That was it. That
was the car I saw.

610
00:38:17,362 --> 00:38:18,839
That must have been the guy.

611
00:38:18,863 --> 00:38:21,242
Just tell me you
saw his license plate.

612
00:38:21,266 --> 00:38:23,010
I saw his license plate,

613
00:38:23,034 --> 00:38:25,663
but it was so fast
I couldn't catch it.

614
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:31,535
Wow.

615
00:38:44,355 --> 00:38:47,086
Come on in. Make
yourself comfortable.

616
00:38:49,794 --> 00:38:51,922
Please.

617
00:38:56,968 --> 00:38:58,746
You know, I really
appreciate you squeezing me

618
00:38:58,770 --> 00:39:00,681
into your schedule
like this, Dr. Lehman.

619
00:39:00,705 --> 00:39:03,368
Well, you did indicate
that it was an emergency.

620
00:39:07,979 --> 00:39:09,971
Could I...?

621
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:13,284
Certainly.

622
00:39:15,486 --> 00:39:18,999
Never pictured myself in a
psychiatrist's office before.

623
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:21,035
I'm a nervous wreck.

624
00:39:21,059 --> 00:39:23,270
I've been shaking
all over the place.

625
00:39:23,294 --> 00:39:28,108
Got butterflies in my
stomach as big as elephants.

626
00:39:28,132 --> 00:39:30,945
Well, any idea where
those butterflies come from?

627
00:39:30,969 --> 00:39:32,179
Maybe.

628
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:35,749
See, I'm an investigator
for Ben Matlock.

629
00:39:35,773 --> 00:39:39,520
The man who's been accused
of murdering Judge Price.

630
00:39:39,544 --> 00:39:42,323
So it's up to me
to find evidence

631
00:39:42,347 --> 00:39:44,058
that proves he didn't do it.

632
00:39:44,082 --> 00:39:45,492
And I'm worried.

633
00:39:45,516 --> 00:39:49,612
I mean, what if I can't do it?

634
00:39:51,222 --> 00:39:53,033
What if I let him down?

635
00:39:53,057 --> 00:39:56,170
Yeah. So I got to thinking,

636
00:39:56,194 --> 00:40:00,207
what if Judge Price was
killed by someone who knew

637
00:40:00,231 --> 00:40:03,210
they could frame Ben
Matlock for the murder?

638
00:40:03,234 --> 00:40:06,347
Like say, one of
the three people

639
00:40:06,371 --> 00:40:08,772
he played golf
with that afternoon.

640
00:40:10,608 --> 00:40:12,099
Get out of here.

641
00:40:13,144 --> 00:40:15,689
Don't I get 50 minutes?

642
00:40:15,713 --> 00:40:17,875
I said get out of here!

643
00:40:22,287 --> 00:40:24,916
You know, I feel better already.

644
00:40:32,330 --> 00:40:36,076
Well, see, he had,
uh, brownish hair,

645
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,378
brownish hair.

646
00:40:37,402 --> 00:40:39,847
About yea high, no
mustache or anything,

647
00:40:39,871 --> 00:40:41,749
and, oh, yeah, he
was strong, muscular.

648
00:40:41,773 --> 00:40:42,950
Very athletic.

649
00:40:42,974 --> 00:40:46,053
And he drove a
kind of a darkish,

650
00:40:46,077 --> 00:40:48,656
darkish, American-made,
midsize car.

651
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:49,924
Don't know about the car,

652
00:40:49,948 --> 00:40:51,325
but the description
sounds like Dave.

653
00:40:51,349 --> 00:40:52,793
He lives in that
motel over there.

654
00:40:52,817 --> 00:40:57,197
Always orders ribs
and wonton soup.

655
00:41:00,024 --> 00:41:01,802
You-you wouldn't
know his room number?

656
00:41:01,826 --> 00:41:04,505
We climb those stairs
often enough. 310.

657
00:41:04,529 --> 00:41:06,140
310.310.

658
00:41:06,164 --> 00:41:08,224
310. Come on.

659
00:41:21,813 --> 00:41:23,907
Anybody there?

660
00:41:30,388 --> 00:41:32,099
- Break down the door.
- Break down the door?

661
00:41:32,123 --> 00:41:33,421
Break down the door!

662
00:41:38,296 --> 00:41:40,007
- Follow him.
- Follow him?

663
00:41:40,031 --> 00:41:41,693
Follow him!

664
00:42:21,939 --> 00:42:23,751
Did-did you see him?

665
00:42:23,775 --> 00:42:26,404
Did you see him?!

666
00:42:50,034 --> 00:42:52,046
Were you that good
a shot in Vietnam?

667
00:42:52,070 --> 00:42:53,247
Better.

668
00:42:53,271 --> 00:42:55,449
I represent Ben Matlock.

669
00:42:55,473 --> 00:42:57,451
I know why you're here.

670
00:42:57,475 --> 00:42:59,853
Arthur Prescott called you.

671
00:42:59,877 --> 00:43:01,221
We're friends...

672
00:43:01,245 --> 00:43:04,425
Me, Art, Gilbert
Lehman, Raymond Price.

673
00:43:04,449 --> 00:43:05,426
We're all friends.

674
00:43:05,450 --> 00:43:06,960
What's the matter,

675
00:43:06,984 --> 00:43:09,196
Art talking too fast when
he explained that to you?

676
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:12,833
Guess I just like hearing
it from the horse's mouth.

677
00:43:12,857 --> 00:43:14,535
Let me tell you something.

678
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:15,602
I got a son.

679
00:43:15,626 --> 00:43:17,538
Four years ago,
he needed surgery.

680
00:43:17,562 --> 00:43:20,240
Even with insurance, the
medical bills would have killed us.

681
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:21,909
Now guess who
paid them off for us?

682
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,845
Raymond Price.

683
00:43:24,869 --> 00:43:27,448
But, like you said, it
was four years ago.

684
00:43:27,472 --> 00:43:32,419
You know, Art seems to
think you're pretty hot stuff.

685
00:43:32,443 --> 00:43:35,777
Now me, I think
you're a pain in the ass.

686
00:43:43,221 --> 00:43:45,866
He, uh, ordered a drink,

687
00:43:45,890 --> 00:43:47,768
told me a Judge Price was dead

688
00:43:47,792 --> 00:43:49,770
and and then
called him a jackass.

689
00:43:49,794 --> 00:43:52,539
Do you always remember things
your customers say so clearly?

690
00:43:52,563 --> 00:43:55,008
Well, I do when
they try to stiff me

691
00:43:55,032 --> 00:43:56,710
for the drinks they order.

692
00:43:56,734 --> 00:43:58,412
So he refused to
pay for his drink?

693
00:43:58,436 --> 00:43:59,580
Yeah. I threw him out.

694
00:43:59,604 --> 00:44:01,148
I suppose an event such as that

695
00:44:01,172 --> 00:44:02,916
would tend to
stick in one's mind.

696
00:44:02,940 --> 00:44:04,718
Thank you.

697
00:44:04,742 --> 00:44:06,472
Your witness, Counselor.

698
00:44:09,113 --> 00:44:12,493
Isn't it likely that another
reason you remember

699
00:44:12,517 --> 00:44:15,295
what he said so clearly was
because of the strange way

700
00:44:15,319 --> 00:44:17,698
he was acting when he
entered your establishment?

701
00:44:17,722 --> 00:44:19,533
What do you mean?

702
00:44:19,557 --> 00:44:21,235
Well, he slurred his words,

703
00:44:21,259 --> 00:44:23,570
he was loud, he staggered.

704
00:44:23,594 --> 00:44:24,972
He acted intoxicated, didn't he?

705
00:44:24,996 --> 00:44:26,640
No.

706
00:44:26,664 --> 00:44:27,908
I beg your pardon?

707
00:44:27,932 --> 00:44:30,511
He seemed a little high maybe,

708
00:44:30,535 --> 00:44:32,980
but he certainly
did not seem drunk.

709
00:44:33,004 --> 00:44:35,349
If he had, I wouldn't
have served him.

710
00:44:35,373 --> 00:44:37,433
Serving drunks is illegal.

711
00:44:41,012 --> 00:44:43,140
No further questions.

712
00:44:52,190 --> 00:44:56,003
Mrs. Hawkins, I'm
real busy right now.

713
00:44:56,027 --> 00:44:57,437
What is it?

714
00:44:57,461 --> 00:44:59,873
You're gonna be in a
lot of trouble, Mr. Matlock.

715
00:44:59,897 --> 00:45:01,842
Gonna be? Gonna be?!

716
00:45:01,866 --> 00:45:04,511
I just want to tell you
how you can avoid it.

717
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:08,015
What you have to do is focus
on reliability and durability.

718
00:45:08,039 --> 00:45:11,919
You'll say "It's not
easy, but I can do it."

719
00:45:11,943 --> 00:45:14,538
Hello? Hello?

720
00:45:15,813 --> 00:45:17,558
Wearing a suit is one thing,

721
00:45:17,582 --> 00:45:20,677
but shaving... I don't know.

722
00:45:22,186 --> 00:45:24,965
Look at it as a
way to leave behind

723
00:45:24,989 --> 00:45:27,601
what you were and begin afresh.

724
00:45:27,625 --> 00:45:28,991
You know what tomorrow is?

725
00:45:30,161 --> 00:45:33,140
The first day of
the rest of your life.

726
00:45:33,164 --> 00:45:35,542
That's really beautiful, Ben.

727
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:37,110
Where did you get that?

728
00:45:37,134 --> 00:45:39,646
Off a greeting card.

729
00:45:39,670 --> 00:45:41,915
Mr. Sloan, would you
please tell the court

730
00:45:41,939 --> 00:45:44,885
what you saw on the
night of October 9?

731
00:45:44,909 --> 00:45:48,055
Well, I saw that man
there... Mr. Matlock...

732
00:45:48,079 --> 00:45:50,023
Go into Angels Tavern.

733
00:45:50,047 --> 00:45:52,226
What else did you see?

734
00:45:52,250 --> 00:45:54,861
And I saw him come
out of Angels Tavern.

735
00:45:54,885 --> 00:45:57,264
No, I mean before that.

736
00:45:57,288 --> 00:45:58,999
Before that?

737
00:45:59,023 --> 00:46:02,669
I was just hanging out,
minding my own business.

738
00:46:02,693 --> 00:46:04,805
Um...

739
00:46:04,829 --> 00:46:07,941
perhaps I'm not
being clear, Mr. Sloan.

740
00:46:07,965 --> 00:46:11,211
When was the first time you
saw Mr. Matlock that night?

741
00:46:11,235 --> 00:46:14,948
You know, when he
went into Angels Tavern.

742
00:46:14,972 --> 00:46:17,117
Prior to that, you
saw Mr. Matlock

743
00:46:17,141 --> 00:46:20,187
being dragged from a car
into a warehouse, did you not?

744
00:46:20,211 --> 00:46:22,389
No.

745
00:46:22,413 --> 00:46:25,659
You saw Mr. Matlock
leave that warehouse

746
00:46:25,683 --> 00:46:27,327
in a drugged
condition, did you not?

747
00:46:27,351 --> 00:46:29,763
I don't know what
you're talking about.

748
00:46:29,787 --> 00:46:30,764
You're lying, Andrew!

749
00:46:30,788 --> 00:46:31,932
Mr. Matlock...

750
00:46:31,956 --> 00:46:33,066
You-you sold out, didn't you?

751
00:46:33,090 --> 00:46:34,468
You did see the man

752
00:46:34,492 --> 00:46:35,569
- I was chasing...
- Mr. Matlock...

753
00:46:35,593 --> 00:46:36,970
Sit down, Ben.

754
00:46:36,994 --> 00:46:38,905
Only instead of blowing
the whistle, you cut a deal

755
00:46:38,929 --> 00:46:40,307
- with him, didn't you?!
- Mr. Matlock, sit down!

756
00:46:40,331 --> 00:46:41,742
- Mr. Matlock, sit down!
- You cut a deal with him!

757
00:46:41,766 --> 00:46:42,809
- Bailiff.
- Sit down, Ben.

758
00:46:42,833 --> 00:46:44,378
He cut a deal with
him, Your Honor.

759
00:46:44,402 --> 00:46:45,612
Mr. Matlock, another
outburst like that,

760
00:46:45,636 --> 00:46:47,281
and I will have you
placed in restraints

761
00:46:47,305 --> 00:46:50,183
for the rest of this
trial. Am I understood?

762
00:46:50,207 --> 00:46:51,585
But he cut a deal with him!

763
00:46:56,814 --> 00:46:59,045
Proceed, Counselor.

764
00:47:00,084 --> 00:47:01,828
No further questions.

765
00:47:01,852 --> 00:47:03,497
Wish to cross?

766
00:47:03,521 --> 00:47:05,699
No, Your Honor.

767
00:47:05,723 --> 00:47:07,089
Witness may step down.

768
00:47:11,429 --> 00:47:14,775
You cut a deal with him,
and I'll get you for that.

769
00:47:14,799 --> 00:47:16,927
Mr. Matlock.

770
00:47:34,452 --> 00:47:35,896
Conrad, they still here?

771
00:47:35,920 --> 00:47:36,997
Yeah, barely.

772
00:47:37,021 --> 00:47:38,785
Come on, let's go around.

773
00:47:58,509 --> 00:48:00,320
When Sloan walked
out of the courthouse,

774
00:48:00,344 --> 00:48:02,522
he hailed a cab and
came straight here.

775
00:48:02,546 --> 00:48:03,878
Recognize his friend?

776
00:48:06,183 --> 00:48:07,928
That's him. That's the killer.

777
00:48:07,952 --> 00:48:09,545
I'll call the police.

778
00:48:12,022 --> 00:48:14,468
All's I want is my money

779
00:48:14,492 --> 00:48:16,723
so I can get out of here.

780
00:48:18,396 --> 00:48:20,440
What's in those things, anyway?

781
00:48:20,464 --> 00:48:22,057
I'll show you.

782
00:48:29,607 --> 00:48:31,371
Andrew!

783
00:49:03,574 --> 00:49:05,719
Conrad, you all right?

784
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:07,507
Yeah...

785
00:49:12,416 --> 00:49:15,847
Well... there goes the killer.

786
00:49:22,827 --> 00:49:24,771
We'll check.

787
00:49:24,795 --> 00:49:27,264
All right, move him in.

788
00:49:34,438 --> 00:49:36,450
People here say his
real name is Walker,

789
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:37,751
Scott Walker.

790
00:49:37,775 --> 00:49:38,919
That's his plane.

791
00:49:38,943 --> 00:49:40,387
According to the
flight plan he filed,

792
00:49:40,411 --> 00:49:42,122
he was headed to Catalina today.

793
00:49:42,146 --> 00:49:44,157
Well, he could be
anywhere by now.

794
00:49:44,181 --> 00:49:45,425
He took that left turn.

795
00:49:45,449 --> 00:49:46,693
Maybe he went
to Central America.

796
00:49:46,717 --> 00:49:48,495
- Think he's smuggling drugs?
- Who knows?

797
00:49:48,519 --> 00:49:50,063
His room was clean as a whistle.

798
00:49:50,087 --> 00:49:52,999
I asked the people at his
motel about his phone bill.

799
00:49:53,023 --> 00:49:54,701
He made four phone
calls in three days

800
00:49:54,725 --> 00:49:57,471
to someone at the Lucinda
Bar in Downtown L.A.

801
00:49:57,495 --> 00:50:01,041
Maybe Conrad
ought to look into that.

802
00:50:01,065 --> 00:50:03,410
I was just thinking that.

803
00:50:03,434 --> 00:50:05,745
Might be interesting
to take a look

804
00:50:05,769 --> 00:50:08,415
at all our suspects'
phone bills.

805
00:50:08,439 --> 00:50:11,551
See if they have a person
or a place in common.

806
00:50:11,575 --> 00:50:14,238
I was just thinking that, too.

807
00:50:27,124 --> 00:50:28,422
Thank you.

808
00:50:30,794 --> 00:50:32,005
Excuse me.

809
00:50:32,029 --> 00:50:33,473
My name is Michelle Thomas.

810
00:50:33,497 --> 00:50:35,609
I'd like to see copies
of the office phone bills

811
00:50:35,633 --> 00:50:37,611
for the past six months,
if you don't mind.

812
00:50:37,635 --> 00:50:39,012
Do you work here?

813
00:50:39,036 --> 00:50:41,581
You haven't been told
about the independent audit

814
00:50:41,605 --> 00:50:43,783
that Watson and Taft
has been hired to perform?

815
00:50:43,807 --> 00:50:45,552
No.

816
00:50:45,576 --> 00:50:47,454
Oh.

817
00:50:47,478 --> 00:50:49,322
Well, the senior
partners are concerned

818
00:50:49,346 --> 00:50:50,590
that the firm's office expenses

819
00:50:50,614 --> 00:50:53,709
seem to be spiraling
out of control.

820
00:50:54,985 --> 00:50:56,830
How far back do
you want me to go?

821
00:50:56,854 --> 00:50:58,698
The last six months.

822
00:50:58,722 --> 00:51:01,201
Okay.

823
00:51:01,225 --> 00:51:04,404
You want 'em, you got 'em.

824
00:51:04,428 --> 00:51:06,006
Have a seat.

825
00:51:06,030 --> 00:51:07,464
Oh, thank you.

826
00:52:01,285 --> 00:52:03,630
How about a beer?

827
00:52:03,654 --> 00:52:05,714
We don't have any.

828
00:52:07,524 --> 00:52:09,993
He's got a beer.

829
00:52:11,028 --> 00:52:13,224
He got the last one.

830
00:52:15,199 --> 00:52:17,930
I see... You don't
serve strangers.

831
00:52:18,969 --> 00:52:21,381
This is a neighborhood bar.

832
00:52:21,405 --> 00:52:23,350
What I really want is a job.

833
00:52:23,374 --> 00:52:24,551
I'm a bartender.

834
00:52:24,575 --> 00:52:26,305
Who do I talk to?

835
00:52:29,146 --> 00:52:30,546
Try the man in the moon.

836
00:52:31,515 --> 00:52:32,792
Ow!

837
00:52:32,816 --> 00:52:34,728
These are dangerous times.

838
00:52:34,752 --> 00:52:36,496
You could break your hand

839
00:52:36,520 --> 00:52:38,565
and leave this place
with nobody to fill in.

840
00:52:38,589 --> 00:52:39,933
You ever think about that?

841
00:52:39,957 --> 00:52:42,335
Hmm?

842
00:52:42,359 --> 00:52:46,039
The problem is, my friend,

843
00:52:46,063 --> 00:52:49,625
my customers prefer drinks
you've probably never heard of.

844
00:52:51,635 --> 00:52:52,967
Try me.

845
00:52:56,507 --> 00:53:01,421
A zombie, a Perfect Rob
Roy and a Suffering Bastard.

846
00:53:01,445 --> 00:53:02,879
Coming up.

847
00:53:52,296 --> 00:53:54,424
Zombie...

848
00:53:56,200 --> 00:53:57,998
Perfect Rob Roy...

849
00:54:00,137 --> 00:54:02,538
Suffering Bastard.

850
00:54:05,709 --> 00:54:08,076
My name is Carlos Berman.

851
00:54:09,713 --> 00:54:12,459
You can call me Carl.

852
00:54:12,483 --> 00:54:15,146
All my employees do.

853
00:54:53,690 --> 00:54:58,287
♪♪

854
00:55:28,959 --> 00:55:31,360
♪♪

855
00:55:59,857 --> 00:56:02,827
♪♪

856
00:56:35,659 --> 00:56:37,003
Well, thanks.

857
00:56:37,027 --> 00:56:38,972
That's very nice of you.

858
00:56:38,996 --> 00:56:41,975
I made a call while I was
out to Watson and Taft,

859
00:56:41,999 --> 00:56:45,445
just to check.

860
00:56:45,469 --> 00:56:47,780
No one would confirm the audit?

861
00:56:47,804 --> 00:56:50,035
That's right.

862
00:56:52,342 --> 00:56:54,187
Well, it's a secret.

863
00:56:54,211 --> 00:56:57,443
No one there has ever heard
of Michelle Thomas either.

864
00:57:00,117 --> 00:57:02,161
I'm an attorney.

865
00:57:02,185 --> 00:57:04,998
I need to find out
as much as I can

866
00:57:05,022 --> 00:57:06,991
about Arthur Prescott.

867
00:57:08,325 --> 00:57:10,203
Are you going to
make trouble for him?

868
00:57:10,227 --> 00:57:13,473
That's not my intent,

869
00:57:13,497 --> 00:57:16,626
but to be honest,
it is a possibility.

870
00:57:17,668 --> 00:57:19,412
Forget his phone bills.

871
00:57:19,436 --> 00:57:22,235
How would you like to
get into his beach house?

872
00:57:24,708 --> 00:57:27,020
You could do that?

873
00:57:27,044 --> 00:57:29,022
1:00 tomorrow.

874
00:57:29,046 --> 00:57:30,690
Pacific Coast Highway to Malibu.

875
00:57:30,714 --> 00:57:31,925
I'll meet you there.

876
00:57:31,949 --> 00:57:34,527
He'll be at lunch.

877
00:57:34,551 --> 00:57:38,097
At the risk of my
sounding ungrateful,

878
00:57:38,121 --> 00:57:39,350
why are you doing this?

879
00:57:41,591 --> 00:57:44,356
He's a pig.

880
00:57:57,641 --> 00:57:59,719
Not good enough.

881
00:57:59,743 --> 00:58:02,736
Out in 48 hours guaranteed,
or I talk to somebody else.

882
00:58:04,648 --> 00:58:07,260
FBI! Everybody stay put!

883
00:58:07,284 --> 00:58:09,879
Keep calm and
nobody will get hurt!

884
00:58:16,793 --> 00:58:18,538
Turn the lights back on!

885
00:58:18,562 --> 00:58:21,464
Turn the damn lights
on or we'll start shooting!

886
00:58:24,067 --> 00:58:26,212
You, put your hands up.

887
00:58:26,236 --> 00:58:27,380
Come out from behind there.

888
00:58:27,404 --> 00:58:28,815
That little trick
with the light switch

889
00:58:28,839 --> 00:58:31,138
has earned you a
night behind bars.

890
00:58:33,577 --> 00:58:37,190
Come on, get up.
Let's go. Come on!

891
00:58:37,214 --> 00:58:41,094
You, too, let's go.

892
00:58:41,118 --> 00:58:42,829
What are you waiting for?

893
00:58:42,853 --> 00:58:46,232
You're the guest of honor.

894
00:58:46,256 --> 00:58:49,035
What's the charge
this time, Agent Wilson?

895
00:58:49,059 --> 00:58:51,337
I thought I'd surprise you.

896
00:58:51,361 --> 00:58:52,505
Let's go.

897
00:59:10,881 --> 00:59:12,679
Hey, what is this?

898
00:59:14,718 --> 00:59:16,829
Where's my phone call?

899
00:59:16,853 --> 00:59:18,947
Don't I get to
talk to my lawyer?

900
00:59:21,691 --> 00:59:22,935
My attorney's on his way.

901
00:59:22,959 --> 00:59:24,689
He'll take care of you.

902
00:59:27,931 --> 00:59:29,909
I appreciate what you did.

903
00:59:29,933 --> 00:59:32,779
Getting rousted is an
inconvenience for me.

904
00:59:32,803 --> 00:59:35,848
For my associate, it
would have been a disaster.

905
00:59:35,872 --> 00:59:38,364
This happens to
you all the time?

906
00:59:40,343 --> 00:59:43,489
As soldiers in the
illustrious war against drugs,

907
00:59:43,513 --> 00:59:45,558
they have a need for an enemy,

908
00:59:45,582 --> 00:59:47,994
someone they can hunt
down, capture, interrogate,

909
00:59:48,018 --> 00:59:49,762
report on to their superiors.

910
00:59:49,786 --> 00:59:52,498
One who will justify their
paychecks and pension plans.

911
00:59:52,522 --> 00:59:53,866
That's you?

912
00:59:53,890 --> 00:59:55,068
I'm tangible, you see.

913
00:59:55,092 --> 00:59:58,529
Poverty and prejudice are not.

914
01:00:00,063 --> 01:00:01,793
Gentlemen...

915
01:00:04,701 --> 01:00:06,479
Let's go, Carlos.

916
01:00:06,503 --> 01:00:08,414
Time to talk.

917
01:00:08,438 --> 01:00:10,783
I'd just as soon have
my attorney present.

918
01:00:10,807 --> 01:00:12,785
Well, he got picked
up on his way over here

919
01:00:12,809 --> 01:00:14,487
for speeding or something.

920
01:00:14,511 --> 01:00:17,413
We're going to have
to start without him.

921
01:00:35,198 --> 01:00:37,910
And the backhand's okay,
but this is not working.

922
01:00:37,934 --> 01:00:39,178
Yeah.

923
01:00:39,202 --> 01:00:40,513
Any net time tomorrow?

924
01:00:40,537 --> 01:00:42,548
Yeah, sure. Just
work on that forehand.

925
01:00:42,572 --> 01:00:44,317
I will, yeah.
That's the problem.

926
01:00:44,341 --> 01:00:46,486
It's just... it's
that elbow I think.

927
01:00:46,510 --> 01:00:48,287
- I don't know. I'm not sure.
- It's the follow-through.

928
01:00:48,311 --> 01:00:50,790
- Uh, Dr. Lehman.
- Hmm?

929
01:00:50,814 --> 01:00:52,191
Ben Matlock.

930
01:00:52,215 --> 01:00:55,094
Uh, catch you later.

931
01:00:55,118 --> 01:00:57,196
We sort of met
on the golf course

932
01:00:57,220 --> 01:00:59,432
- the day Judge Price was killed.
- Yeah.

933
01:00:59,456 --> 01:01:01,200
Could I talk with
you for a minute?

934
01:01:01,224 --> 01:01:04,003
Your investigators
already paid me a visit.

935
01:01:04,027 --> 01:01:05,505
I know, but that
was something else.

936
01:01:05,529 --> 01:01:06,572
Sit down, please.

937
01:01:06,596 --> 01:01:07,928
Have some lemonade.

938
01:01:12,035 --> 01:01:16,516
Um, there's a drug, oxynol,

939
01:01:16,540 --> 01:01:18,951
it's a hallucinogen.

940
01:01:18,975 --> 01:01:20,987
It was developed
secretly by our government

941
01:01:21,011 --> 01:01:24,657
in the early '60s, to
make the enemy talk.

942
01:01:24,681 --> 01:01:26,259
I'm familiar with it.

943
01:01:26,283 --> 01:01:28,895
If I'm not mistaken,

944
01:01:28,919 --> 01:01:32,899
the only place it was actually
used was in Cambodia.

945
01:01:32,923 --> 01:01:38,404
Um, Special Forces were sent
in to-to set up for an invasion.

946
01:01:38,428 --> 01:01:40,439
I believe mostly
Green Beret units.

947
01:01:40,463 --> 01:01:43,476
Could you tell me about it?

948
01:01:43,500 --> 01:01:44,844
Well, I could try.

949
01:01:44,868 --> 01:01:48,381
Uh, suppose a person
were injected with it,

950
01:01:48,405 --> 01:01:49,749
what would happen?

951
01:01:49,773 --> 01:01:54,220
He'd become disoriented,
unable to think clearly.

952
01:01:54,244 --> 01:01:58,257
He'd suffer short-term memory
loss, be very suggestible.

953
01:01:58,281 --> 01:02:00,560
Would he appear to be drunk?

954
01:02:00,584 --> 01:02:03,462
Extremely.

955
01:02:03,486 --> 01:02:05,331
Have you ever had
occasion to use oxynol

956
01:02:05,355 --> 01:02:06,699
on one of your patients?

957
01:02:06,723 --> 01:02:08,868
Nope.

958
01:02:08,892 --> 01:02:11,384
Thanks for the lemonade.

959
01:02:53,203 --> 01:02:54,680
Give him the keys.

960
01:02:54,704 --> 01:02:55,781
What are you talking about?

961
01:02:55,805 --> 01:02:59,085
Ah, come on...
All right, all right.

962
01:02:59,109 --> 01:03:00,805
Get in!

963
01:03:52,095 --> 01:03:53,472
Hello, Michelle.

964
01:03:53,496 --> 01:03:55,941
I know this isn't
what you expected

965
01:03:55,965 --> 01:03:58,491
but come in, please.

966
01:04:08,211 --> 01:04:10,156
This was all a setup?

967
01:04:10,180 --> 01:04:13,826
Linda, the woman you spoke
to in the accounting office,

968
01:04:13,850 --> 01:04:16,996
she's, uh, well, she came
straight to me that day.

969
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:18,998
She's a very loyal girl.

970
01:04:19,022 --> 01:04:20,900
Why didn't you come to
me? I have nothing to hide.

971
01:04:20,924 --> 01:04:22,835
It was your idea to come here?

972
01:04:22,859 --> 01:04:25,204
Well, I thought it'd
give us a chance

973
01:04:25,228 --> 01:04:27,340
to get to know each other.

974
01:04:29,065 --> 01:04:31,977
- I don't think so.
- Oh, come on.

975
01:04:32,001 --> 01:04:33,479
We'll talk, we'll eat,

976
01:04:33,503 --> 01:04:35,948
and then later I'll show
you all my phone bills.

977
01:04:35,972 --> 01:04:38,818
Come on, a little crab
salad, some Chardonnay?

978
01:04:38,842 --> 01:04:41,710
Let me take your jacket.

979
01:04:55,825 --> 01:04:57,136
Make it fast.

980
01:04:57,160 --> 01:04:59,338
I don't know how
long I can keep her.

981
01:04:59,362 --> 01:05:02,141
Call me as soon as you get back.

982
01:05:02,165 --> 01:05:05,135
Right.

983
01:05:35,031 --> 01:05:38,024
♪♪

984
01:06:07,230 --> 01:06:08,641
Don't you think so?

985
01:06:08,665 --> 01:06:11,877
If you like this one, this...

986
01:06:11,901 --> 01:06:15,314
Uh, uh, I've got to
use your bathroom.

987
01:06:15,338 --> 01:06:17,716
I'm sorry, our restroom
is not open to the public.

988
01:06:17,740 --> 01:06:19,051
But I'm...

989
01:06:19,075 --> 01:06:21,353
I'm diabetic and
I've got to take a pill.

990
01:06:21,377 --> 01:06:24,490
I could go into insulin
shock any minute.

991
01:06:24,514 --> 01:06:26,959
I'm sorry.

992
01:06:26,983 --> 01:06:29,128
The last time this happened,

993
01:06:29,152 --> 01:06:32,031
I skipped the shock part
altogether and went straight

994
01:06:32,055 --> 01:06:35,000
into a coma right
there in the shoe store.

995
01:06:35,024 --> 01:06:37,736
Behind the counter
and to your left.

996
01:06:37,760 --> 01:06:39,388
- Thank you, thank you.
- Sure.

997
01:06:42,632 --> 01:06:45,611
You cut us off now,
we'll be destroyed forever.

998
01:06:45,635 --> 01:06:48,080
It's a lost cause, Rahmad.

999
01:06:48,104 --> 01:06:50,516
Maybe it's time
you admitted it, too.

1000
01:06:50,540 --> 01:06:52,518
You gave your word.

1001
01:06:52,542 --> 01:06:54,587
For six months we've
been giving you support.

1002
01:06:54,611 --> 01:06:55,821
What have we got to show for it?

1003
01:06:55,845 --> 01:06:58,123
Nothing. You squandered it.

1004
01:06:58,147 --> 01:06:59,859
Now it's getting too hot.

1005
01:06:59,883 --> 01:07:01,460
This is the end of it.

1006
01:07:07,724 --> 01:07:09,401
Caught him listening
outside the door.

1007
01:07:09,425 --> 01:07:10,703
Anybody know who he is?

1008
01:07:12,128 --> 01:07:14,529
Unfortunately, I do.

1009
01:07:19,168 --> 01:07:23,015
I caught 27 trout that day.

1010
01:07:23,039 --> 01:07:25,951
That is almost
five fish an hour.

1011
01:07:27,510 --> 01:07:31,490
Mr. Prescott, you've talked
about everything under the sun,

1012
01:07:31,514 --> 01:07:33,959
and I realize you
love fly-fishing,

1013
01:07:33,983 --> 01:07:36,962
but I get the feeling you're
being deliberately evasive.

1014
01:07:36,986 --> 01:07:38,531
Evasive, no.

1015
01:07:38,555 --> 01:07:42,067
I'm, uh, just a little nervous.

1016
01:07:42,091 --> 01:07:45,371
I, uh, I like you.

1017
01:07:45,395 --> 01:07:47,239
What about the phone bills?

1018
01:07:47,263 --> 01:07:51,724
Look, why don't we discuss
that over some dessert, huh?

1019
01:07:53,770 --> 01:07:56,282
Mr. Prescott, would you
please get my jacket?

1020
01:07:59,943 --> 01:08:01,070
Just a second.

1021
01:08:09,752 --> 01:08:11,263
Hello?

1022
01:08:11,287 --> 01:08:13,499
Yeah, look, can I
get right back to you?

1023
01:08:13,523 --> 01:08:15,434
Thanks.

1024
01:08:15,458 --> 01:08:17,984
I'll get your jacket.

1025
01:08:31,908 --> 01:08:33,519
Did you find anything?

1026
01:08:33,543 --> 01:08:36,689
There's nothing in her room that
incriminates you or anyone else.

1027
01:08:36,713 --> 01:08:38,875
We're home free.

1028
01:08:42,885 --> 01:08:44,330
Here you go.

1029
01:08:44,354 --> 01:08:45,631
Thanks. And thanks for lunch.

1030
01:08:45,655 --> 01:08:47,232
The salad was terrific.

1031
01:08:47,256 --> 01:08:49,816
Well, I'll be sure to
tell my housekeeper.

1032
01:08:57,634 --> 01:08:59,178
Oh, I almost forgot.

1033
01:08:59,202 --> 01:09:01,213
I wanted to ask
you about oxynol.

1034
01:09:01,237 --> 01:09:02,581
About what?

1035
01:09:02,605 --> 01:09:05,084
The drug you had
access to in Vietnam.

1036
01:09:05,108 --> 01:09:08,053
Oxynol, the hallucinogen.

1037
01:09:08,077 --> 01:09:12,024
The problem is I really
don't have time right now.

1038
01:09:12,048 --> 01:09:13,292
Guess it'll have to wait.

1039
01:09:13,316 --> 01:09:15,683
Like the phone bills.

1040
01:10:48,544 --> 01:10:50,823
Remember your name yet?

1041
01:10:50,847 --> 01:10:57,496
Uh... Uh, it's B-Bat...
Bat... Uh, Batl...

1042
01:10:57,520 --> 01:11:00,099
L... No, no, no.

1043
01:11:00,123 --> 01:11:03,869
Uh, wait, it's Ben, Ben Matlock.

1044
01:11:03,893 --> 01:11:06,205
- Benjamin Matlock?
- Yeah.

1045
01:11:06,229 --> 01:11:08,874
This is that lawyer accused
of killing Judge Price.

1046
01:11:08,898 --> 01:11:10,209
Seedy looking bum.

1047
01:11:10,233 --> 01:11:13,863
Do you know my mother
wanted me to go to law school?

1048
01:11:30,720 --> 01:11:33,417
Ben?

1049
01:11:34,457 --> 01:11:37,256
Ben?

1050
01:11:42,198 --> 01:11:43,632
Conrad?

1051
01:11:46,702 --> 01:11:50,036
Conrad?

1052
01:11:53,009 --> 01:11:55,308
Where are you guys?

1053
01:11:57,346 --> 01:11:59,558
So, how did it go?

1054
01:11:59,582 --> 01:12:01,574
The usual.

1055
01:12:03,186 --> 01:12:04,797
Wilson tried to get me
to tell him what I know

1056
01:12:04,821 --> 01:12:08,200
about drug trafficking in the
city and as usual, he failed.

1057
01:12:08,224 --> 01:12:11,503
I must admit, I was glad

1058
01:12:11,527 --> 01:12:14,190
when my attorney
finally showed up.

1059
01:12:15,231 --> 01:12:16,642
You want something?

1060
01:12:16,666 --> 01:12:18,143
Coffee.

1061
01:12:18,167 --> 01:12:19,411
Okay.

1062
01:12:19,435 --> 01:12:21,013
Coming up.

1063
01:12:21,037 --> 01:12:22,614
My attorney tells me

1064
01:12:22,638 --> 01:12:24,850
that you have no criminal
record in California.

1065
01:12:24,874 --> 01:12:28,453
I've kept my nose clean...

1066
01:12:28,477 --> 01:12:30,789
and I'm not from California.

1067
01:12:30,813 --> 01:12:32,558
Then how did you
find out about my bar?

1068
01:12:32,582 --> 01:12:34,881
- Friends.
- Who?

1069
01:12:36,385 --> 01:12:38,831
I was told that if an
enterprising type of guy

1070
01:12:38,855 --> 01:12:40,098
wanted to get
ahead in this town,

1071
01:12:40,122 --> 01:12:41,533
this was the place to come.

1072
01:12:41,557 --> 01:12:45,270
You want names,
I don't do names.

1073
01:12:45,294 --> 01:12:48,040
I forget names as
soon as I hear them.

1074
01:12:50,299 --> 01:12:52,427
An enterprising young
man with a clean nose.

1075
01:12:54,136 --> 01:12:56,782
You could prove
very useful to me.

1076
01:12:56,806 --> 01:12:58,399
Yeah?

1077
01:13:00,343 --> 01:13:02,020
I have some business
to attend to this evening.

1078
01:13:02,044 --> 01:13:04,423
- Why don't you come along?
- Okay.

1079
01:13:04,447 --> 01:13:08,578
I'll call my girlfriend, we
were gonna go to dinner.

1080
01:13:10,086 --> 01:13:11,987
Business before pleasure.

1081
01:13:14,724 --> 01:13:17,523
Call her afterwards.

1082
01:13:23,833 --> 01:13:26,011
All right, come on, stay
in line, keep moving.

1083
01:13:26,035 --> 01:13:28,027
My lawyer here yet?

1084
01:13:33,776 --> 01:13:35,888
Hey.

1085
01:13:35,912 --> 01:13:36,989
- Hey.
- Hmm?

1086
01:13:37,013 --> 01:13:39,057
- Hey, wake up.
- Hmm! Hmm.

1087
01:13:39,081 --> 01:13:41,393
Got a visitor.

1088
01:13:41,417 --> 01:13:43,909
- Hey!
- Hmm...

1089
01:13:58,167 --> 01:14:00,279
Are you all right?

1090
01:14:00,303 --> 01:14:01,896
Here, sit down.

1091
01:14:03,339 --> 01:14:05,684
What happened?

1092
01:14:05,708 --> 01:14:07,352
Somebody drugged you again.

1093
01:14:07,376 --> 01:14:08,854
Only this time, you went

1094
01:14:08,878 --> 01:14:12,190
wandering around in the
middle of the San Diego freeway.

1095
01:14:12,214 --> 01:14:14,159
I did?

1096
01:14:14,183 --> 01:14:16,061
Yeah.

1097
01:14:16,085 --> 01:14:18,030
Highway Patrol turned you
over to Lieutenant Myerson.

1098
01:14:18,054 --> 01:14:20,032
He's the one who called me.

1099
01:14:20,056 --> 01:14:21,667
You'd passed out by then.

1100
01:14:21,691 --> 01:14:23,802
Ooh, see that?

1101
01:14:23,826 --> 01:14:28,807
They shot me up and
threw me on a freeway?

1102
01:14:28,831 --> 01:14:30,275
Ben, who did this to you?

1103
01:14:30,299 --> 01:14:31,643
Where were you today?

1104
01:14:31,667 --> 01:14:36,648
Well, I talked to Dr. Lehman
at the country club,

1105
01:14:36,672 --> 01:14:39,418
and followed him
to a clothing store

1106
01:14:39,442 --> 01:14:43,422
and I-I heard him
arguing with somebody.

1107
01:14:43,446 --> 01:14:45,190
Then what?

1108
01:14:45,214 --> 01:14:49,127
I don't know. Somebody
must've hit me.

1109
01:14:49,151 --> 01:14:52,431
Ooh, left a goose
egg the size of Ohio.

1110
01:14:54,623 --> 01:14:57,102
You think Dr. Lehman
drugged you?

1111
01:14:57,126 --> 01:14:58,837
Well, he could've.

1112
01:14:58,861 --> 01:15:02,841
Could've been any one
of those ex-Green Berets.

1113
01:15:02,865 --> 01:15:04,876
They all knew about the drug.

1114
01:15:04,900 --> 01:15:07,412
I think they were all involved.

1115
01:15:07,436 --> 01:15:09,081
Listen to this.

1116
01:15:09,105 --> 01:15:11,016
I was in Arthur Prescott's
beach house today.

1117
01:15:11,040 --> 01:15:13,885
I borrowed the tape that
was in his answering machine.

1118
01:15:13,909 --> 01:15:17,155
We're getting together
at the warehouse.

1119
01:15:17,179 --> 01:15:18,857
North Venice, 6:00 p.m.

1120
01:15:20,316 --> 01:15:21,626
I interviewed Daryl Wilson.

1121
01:15:21,650 --> 01:15:23,642
I'm willing to bet that was him.

1122
01:15:25,621 --> 01:15:27,132
6:00. That's...

1123
01:15:27,156 --> 01:15:33,138
That's no more than a
couple of hours away.

1124
01:15:33,162 --> 01:15:35,807
We're getting together
at the warehouse.

1125
01:15:35,831 --> 01:15:39,011
North Venice, 6:00 p.m.

1126
01:15:39,035 --> 01:15:41,279
That's it?

1127
01:15:41,303 --> 01:15:42,614
Short and sweet.

1128
01:15:42,638 --> 01:15:45,317
It could've been an
invitation to a party.

1129
01:15:45,341 --> 01:15:47,652
I'm almost positive the
man who left that message

1130
01:15:47,676 --> 01:15:49,654
was Daryl Wilson.

1131
01:15:49,678 --> 01:15:53,158
- The FBI agent?
- Yep.

1132
01:15:53,182 --> 01:15:55,527
You guys are great.

1133
01:15:55,551 --> 01:15:57,462
Where did you get the tape?

1134
01:15:57,486 --> 01:15:59,264
- I borrowed it.
- She borrowed it.

1135
01:15:59,288 --> 01:16:00,899
Lieutenant,

1136
01:16:00,923 --> 01:16:04,436
I'm telling you something
very big, very important

1137
01:16:04,460 --> 01:16:06,538
is gonna take place at that
warehouse this afternoon,

1138
01:16:06,562 --> 01:16:08,206
and I intend to be there.

1139
01:16:08,230 --> 01:16:10,909
It's a free country.

1140
01:16:10,933 --> 01:16:14,346
Could be pretty embarrassing,

1141
01:16:14,370 --> 01:16:19,551
if what I find out
blows this case apart.

1142
01:16:19,575 --> 01:16:21,153
I'll take my chances.

1143
01:16:21,177 --> 01:16:23,789
Reporters calling from
all over the country.

1144
01:16:23,813 --> 01:16:26,758
I'll have to tell them that
apathy on the part of a certain

1145
01:16:26,782 --> 01:16:30,562
police lieutenant forced me to
take matters into my own hands.

1146
01:16:30,586 --> 01:16:35,991
You spell your last
name with one "E" or two?

1147
01:17:44,260 --> 01:17:46,505
Should be here right away.

1148
01:18:02,545 --> 01:18:05,657
What do you know...
It's Carlos Berman.

1149
01:18:05,681 --> 01:18:09,094
- Yeah. Yeah.
- He's a very big drug boy.

1150
01:18:09,118 --> 01:18:11,019
Now this is getting interesting.

1151
01:18:27,836 --> 01:18:29,915
An FBI agent is involved.

1152
01:18:29,939 --> 01:18:31,283
Yeah, up to his ears.

1153
01:18:31,307 --> 01:18:33,970
The guy with him
killed Judge Price.

1154
01:18:52,094 --> 01:18:53,905
What the hell is he doing here?!

1155
01:18:53,929 --> 01:18:56,875
Conrad! Get down!

1156
01:18:56,899 --> 01:18:59,300
- Police officers, freeze!
- Hold it!

1157
01:19:24,093 --> 01:19:26,438
Hold your fire!

1158
01:19:26,462 --> 01:19:29,830
- Hold your fire!
- Hold your fire!

1159
01:19:34,536 --> 01:19:36,748
All right, everybody,

1160
01:19:36,772 --> 01:19:39,435
come out with your hands up now.

1161
01:19:42,978 --> 01:19:44,489
Drop your weapons!

1162
01:19:44,513 --> 01:19:46,191
Now keep them high!

1163
01:19:46,215 --> 01:19:48,184
Keep them where we can see them!

1164
01:19:53,055 --> 01:19:54,432
Arms behind your back!

1165
01:19:54,456 --> 01:19:56,334
Conrad, are you all right?

1166
01:19:56,358 --> 01:19:58,536
- Oh, yeah, I'm fine.
- What the hell you doing here?

1167
01:19:58,560 --> 01:20:00,105
When I saw you
get out of that car,

1168
01:20:00,129 --> 01:20:01,439
I thought I was seeing things.

1169
01:20:01,463 --> 01:20:03,989
- Ben.
- What?

1170
01:20:29,792 --> 01:20:32,704
So, they're all set to give
Berman 500 pounds of cocaine,

1171
01:20:32,728 --> 01:20:36,574
and he's all set to give them
close to $8 million in cash.

1172
01:20:36,598 --> 01:20:38,343
Some system.

1173
01:20:40,069 --> 01:20:41,513
Hello?

1174
01:20:41,537 --> 01:20:43,281
Hey, Mrs. Hawkins. Yeah,
hang on, he's right here.

1175
01:20:43,305 --> 01:20:45,884
Yeah, Mrs. Hawkins?

1176
01:20:45,908 --> 01:20:47,052
Good news, Mr. Matlock.

1177
01:20:47,076 --> 01:20:48,753
Now, don't hang
up, listen to this.

1178
01:20:48,777 --> 01:20:50,055
Here's your horoscope for today.

1179
01:20:50,079 --> 01:20:51,523
Ready?

1180
01:20:51,547 --> 01:20:53,858
"A new day is dawning.

1181
01:20:53,882 --> 01:20:56,094
"Time to revitalize
and refurbish.

1182
01:20:56,118 --> 01:20:57,829
Brighten the corner
where you are."

1183
01:20:57,853 --> 01:21:01,266
Mrs. Hawkins... So,
you know what I did?

1184
01:21:01,290 --> 01:21:03,735
I bought new drapes and
a new spread and sheets

1185
01:21:03,759 --> 01:21:06,771
and towels at Macy's, and I
charged them to your account.

1186
01:21:06,795 --> 01:21:09,374
Luckily, they were
having a white sale.

1187
01:21:09,398 --> 01:21:12,077
Mrs. Hawkins, you had
no business going out...

1188
01:21:12,101 --> 01:21:13,545
Hello?

1189
01:21:13,569 --> 01:21:15,213
Hello?!

1190
01:21:16,839 --> 01:21:18,216
I'll shut up.

1191
01:21:18,240 --> 01:21:21,920
Now, let's see,

1192
01:21:21,944 --> 01:21:24,589
I guess... I guess the
way these guys worked...

1193
01:21:26,615 --> 01:21:28,126
Hello?

1194
01:21:28,150 --> 01:21:30,128
I guess the way
they worked was...

1195
01:21:30,152 --> 01:21:32,697
they'd sell their
guns for-for drugs,

1196
01:21:32,721 --> 01:21:34,432
and then this fellow, Walker,

1197
01:21:34,456 --> 01:21:37,202
would smuggle the drugs
up from Central America

1198
01:21:37,226 --> 01:21:38,603
in that plane of his,

1199
01:21:38,627 --> 01:21:40,939
and he'd get word
to Daryl Wilson,

1200
01:21:40,963 --> 01:21:43,608
and this Wilson then
would pretend to roust

1201
01:21:43,632 --> 01:21:46,244
Carlos Berman so the
two of them could set up

1202
01:21:46,268 --> 01:21:48,747
transfer, and then Wilson
could call the others

1203
01:21:48,771 --> 01:21:51,316
with the time and the place,
you know, the warehouse.

1204
01:21:51,340 --> 01:21:53,118
That was Lieutenant Myerson.

1205
01:21:53,142 --> 01:21:56,688
He said the bullet that
killed Scott Walker was a .45.

1206
01:21:56,712 --> 01:21:58,523
Did you see a .45?

1207
01:21:58,547 --> 01:21:59,724
The police were carrying

1208
01:21:59,748 --> 01:22:02,293
nine millimeter
Berettas and shotguns.

1209
01:22:02,317 --> 01:22:05,530
Carlos Berman's men
were carrying Uzis.

1210
01:22:05,554 --> 01:22:07,098
Well, if he was shot with a .45,

1211
01:22:07,122 --> 01:22:09,557
somebody there
must've had a .45.

1212
01:22:21,703 --> 01:22:23,248
Hello, Mr. Prescott.

1213
01:22:23,272 --> 01:22:25,550
Michelle, what brings you here?

1214
01:22:25,574 --> 01:22:27,752
As I recall from that
picture you showed me,

1215
01:22:27,776 --> 01:22:29,988
you and your friends
carried .45s in Vietnam?

1216
01:22:30,012 --> 01:22:32,123
I'm not gonna deny that.

1217
01:22:32,147 --> 01:22:33,792
Still have yours?

1218
01:22:33,816 --> 01:22:36,194
Yes.

1219
01:22:36,218 --> 01:22:38,696
I have a subpoena for it.

1220
01:22:38,720 --> 01:22:41,900
Would you turn it over
to Officer Landau, please?

1221
01:22:41,924 --> 01:22:45,224
Certainly.

1222
01:22:53,268 --> 01:22:57,364
I understand the party you
were at last night got pretty wild.

1223
01:22:58,407 --> 01:23:01,104
No comment.

1224
01:23:06,415 --> 01:23:08,059
You keep it in your office?

1225
01:23:08,083 --> 01:23:10,094
Some of my patients
tend to get violent.

1226
01:23:10,118 --> 01:23:12,831
- You never know.
- So you're always prepared.

1227
01:23:12,855 --> 01:23:14,999
That's how I got
through Vietnam.

1228
01:23:15,023 --> 01:23:17,235
Luck had something
to do with that, Doctor.

1229
01:23:17,259 --> 01:23:19,057
I sure hope yours
hasn't run out.

1230
01:23:22,297 --> 01:23:24,275
What do you want it for?

1231
01:23:24,299 --> 01:23:26,845
Come to court
tomorrow and you'll see.

1232
01:23:26,869 --> 01:23:29,314
I heard the department
kind of laid you off.

1233
01:23:29,338 --> 01:23:33,184
Well, I'll be reinstated just
as soon as this is cleared up.

1234
01:23:33,208 --> 01:23:34,870
Now get the hell out.

1235
01:23:42,150 --> 01:23:44,395
Sit down. There you go.

1236
01:23:44,419 --> 01:23:48,533
Well...
- what is this?
- Open it.

1237
01:23:50,792 --> 01:23:53,137
Oh.

1238
01:23:53,161 --> 01:23:55,974
It's beautiful.

1239
01:23:55,998 --> 01:23:58,343
Oh.

1240
01:23:58,367 --> 01:24:01,565
All right, Ben, what's going on?

1241
01:24:02,671 --> 01:24:04,682
Well, that's just my
way of thanking you

1242
01:24:04,706 --> 01:24:06,084
for dropping everything at home

1243
01:24:06,108 --> 01:24:08,520
and flying out
here to help me out.

1244
01:24:08,544 --> 01:24:11,623
You're welcome, but it's my job.

1245
01:24:12,981 --> 01:24:15,059
You're a wonderful
lawyer, Michelle.

1246
01:24:15,083 --> 01:24:16,779
You're smart, capable.

1247
01:24:17,819 --> 01:24:19,163
Of course, you know that.

1248
01:24:19,187 --> 01:24:20,965
Thank you.

1249
01:24:20,989 --> 01:24:24,469
And-and you know
that I know that.

1250
01:24:24,493 --> 01:24:26,905
Yeah.

1251
01:24:26,929 --> 01:24:29,023
Ben, what is going on?

1252
01:24:31,900 --> 01:24:34,312
You're gonna hate this.

1253
01:24:34,336 --> 01:24:36,532
How do you know
until you tell me?

1254
01:24:37,573 --> 01:24:40,385
I want to take over
my own defense.

1255
01:24:40,409 --> 01:24:44,055
Now, now, this is
no reflection on you.

1256
01:24:44,079 --> 01:24:45,356
You're a wonderful lawyer.

1257
01:24:45,380 --> 01:24:46,791
Smart and capable.

1258
01:24:46,815 --> 01:24:48,226
But did you always tell me

1259
01:24:48,250 --> 01:24:50,194
that a lawyer who
defends himself has a fool

1260
01:24:50,218 --> 01:24:52,497
- for a client?
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

1261
01:24:52,521 --> 01:24:55,500
And-and-and most
of the time, that's true.

1262
01:24:55,524 --> 01:24:57,068
But this is different.

1263
01:24:57,092 --> 01:24:58,136
What's different is that

1264
01:24:58,160 --> 01:24:59,571
you don't trust
me to defend you.

1265
01:24:59,595 --> 01:25:01,839
I knew it, I knew it, I knew it.

1266
01:25:01,863 --> 01:25:04,108
I-I-I knew you'd think that way.

1267
01:25:04,132 --> 01:25:05,810
What else would I think?

1268
01:25:05,834 --> 01:25:08,046
Michelle, this has
nothing to do with you.

1269
01:25:08,070 --> 01:25:10,548
It's just with me.

1270
01:25:10,572 --> 01:25:14,018
Oh, Ben, you're
not making sense.

1271
01:25:14,042 --> 01:25:15,620
I always make sense.

1272
01:25:15,644 --> 01:25:17,889
I'm a rational, reasonable man.

1273
01:25:17,913 --> 01:25:20,425
Then why do you
want to defend yourself?

1274
01:25:20,449 --> 01:25:21,793
All right.

1275
01:25:21,817 --> 01:25:23,728
One, I know all the facts.

1276
01:25:23,752 --> 01:25:25,697
Two, I'm fully prepared.

1277
01:25:25,721 --> 01:25:29,000
Three, I'm totally objective.

1278
01:25:29,024 --> 01:25:30,802
And four, some lowlife jackass

1279
01:25:30,826 --> 01:25:32,704
is trying to frame
me with murder,

1280
01:25:32,728 --> 01:25:34,906
and I'll not get another
decent night's sleep

1281
01:25:34,930 --> 01:25:38,423
until I personally pin
his hide to the wall.

1282
01:25:39,468 --> 01:25:41,779
That's really rational, Ben.

1283
01:25:41,803 --> 01:25:43,881
Good.

1284
01:25:43,905 --> 01:25:45,216
I'm glad you understand.

1285
01:25:45,240 --> 01:25:48,086
We make a wonderful team.

1286
01:25:54,616 --> 01:25:56,561
Your Honor, at this time,

1287
01:25:56,585 --> 01:25:59,163
Mr. Matlock would like to
assume his own defense.

1288
01:25:59,187 --> 01:26:02,033
As you're aware, my client is
a member of the California Bar

1289
01:26:02,057 --> 01:26:05,069
with a great deal of
experience in criminal law.

1290
01:26:05,093 --> 01:26:06,738
You are aware of the seriousness

1291
01:26:06,762 --> 01:26:08,306
of the charges against
you, Mr. Matlock,

1292
01:26:08,330 --> 01:26:09,407
as well as the dangers

1293
01:26:09,431 --> 01:26:10,808
of representing
yourself in this matter?

1294
01:26:10,832 --> 01:26:12,176
Yea, sir, I am.

1295
01:26:12,200 --> 01:26:14,646
I've tried to dissuade
my client, Your Honor,

1296
01:26:14,670 --> 01:26:16,347
but Mr. Matlock insists.

1297
01:26:16,371 --> 01:26:17,849
It's your decision.

1298
01:26:17,873 --> 01:26:19,550
Call your first witness.

1299
01:26:19,574 --> 01:26:21,133
I call Arthur Prescott.

1300
01:26:25,180 --> 01:26:28,393
You, Dr. Gilbert Lehman,

1301
01:26:28,417 --> 01:26:32,597
FBI Agent Daryl Wilson and
the deceased, Judge Price,

1302
01:26:32,621 --> 01:26:34,699
all served in Vietnam
together, didn't you?

1303
01:26:34,723 --> 01:26:36,034
That's correct.

1304
01:26:36,058 --> 01:26:39,671
And you spent much of
the time while you were there

1305
01:26:39,695 --> 01:26:41,939
behind enemy lines,

1306
01:26:41,963 --> 01:26:44,776
risking your lives for
your country, didn't you?

1307
01:26:44,800 --> 01:26:47,245
Well, we did our jobs, yes.

1308
01:26:47,269 --> 01:26:48,613
Yeah.

1309
01:26:48,637 --> 01:26:54,152
And when it became
apparent that the United States

1310
01:26:54,176 --> 01:26:57,622
had failed to achieve what
you were willing to die for,

1311
01:26:57,646 --> 01:27:00,692
what so many had died for,

1312
01:27:00,716 --> 01:27:03,261
how did you feel, betrayed?

1313
01:27:03,285 --> 01:27:05,563
Well, it's hard to
feel your friends

1314
01:27:05,587 --> 01:27:07,432
are dying for
nothing, Mr. Matlock.

1315
01:27:07,456 --> 01:27:09,934
- Yes, I felt betrayed.
- Yeah.

1316
01:27:09,958 --> 01:27:14,038
"I believe the government
of the United States

1317
01:27:14,062 --> 01:27:16,407
"reneged on its
inherent obligation

1318
01:27:16,431 --> 01:27:19,277
"to democracy in Vietnam

1319
01:27:19,301 --> 01:27:20,978
"and has been reneging
on that obligation

1320
01:27:21,002 --> 01:27:24,549
in countries all over
the world ever since."

1321
01:27:24,573 --> 01:27:25,683
Is that how you felt?

1322
01:27:25,707 --> 01:27:27,485
If I'm not mistaken,

1323
01:27:27,509 --> 01:27:30,221
you just quoted from a
speech made by Raymond Price

1324
01:27:30,245 --> 01:27:34,092
about a year ago at
the local Bar Association.

1325
01:27:34,116 --> 01:27:37,562
That's true, but those are
your sentiments, aren't they?

1326
01:27:37,586 --> 01:27:39,831
I suppose they are, yes.

1327
01:27:39,855 --> 01:27:44,135
And when the congress
cut off all military supplies

1328
01:27:44,159 --> 01:27:47,105
to the forces of democracy
struggling in Central America,

1329
01:27:47,129 --> 01:27:48,306
how did that make you feel?

1330
01:27:48,330 --> 01:27:50,708
I was angry.

1331
01:27:50,732 --> 01:27:54,445
So angry, you decided to do
something about it, didn't you?

1332
01:27:54,469 --> 01:27:55,980
What do you mean?

1333
01:27:56,004 --> 01:27:58,015
You and your friends,
those same four,

1334
01:27:58,039 --> 01:28:04,188
used your military connections
to procure field artillery,

1335
01:28:04,212 --> 01:28:08,459
and you sold that artillery
covertly and illegally

1336
01:28:08,483 --> 01:28:11,562
to the forces you backed in
Central America, didn't you?

1337
01:28:11,586 --> 01:28:13,164
- Of course not.
- Only your fighters

1338
01:28:13,188 --> 01:28:17,635
didn't pay you with money,
they paid you with cocaine,

1339
01:28:17,659 --> 01:28:21,773
which you in turn sold
to... Carlos Berman...

1340
01:28:21,797 --> 01:28:24,242
A man with whom you
rendezvoused two nights ago.

1341
01:28:24,266 --> 01:28:25,676
Isn't that right?

1342
01:28:25,700 --> 01:28:29,547
I'm afraid I'll have to refuse
to answer that question

1343
01:28:29,571 --> 01:28:30,848
on the grounds that it
might tend to incriminate me.

1344
01:28:30,872 --> 01:28:33,951
What did you do with
all the millions of dollars

1345
01:28:33,975 --> 01:28:35,553
you made in the
last couple years

1346
01:28:35,577 --> 01:28:36,988
with such transactions?

1347
01:28:37,012 --> 01:28:39,357
I have to refuse to answer
that question as well

1348
01:28:39,381 --> 01:28:41,759
- on the grounds it might tend to...
- Okay, okay, okay,

1349
01:28:41,783 --> 01:28:43,127
okay, okay, okay.

1350
01:28:43,151 --> 01:28:44,762
Answer me this.

1351
01:28:44,786 --> 01:28:47,165
You didn't do it
for profit, did you?

1352
01:28:47,189 --> 01:28:48,666
You were patriots.

1353
01:28:48,690 --> 01:28:53,571
The four of you, as a group,
in the last year and a half

1354
01:28:53,595 --> 01:28:56,607
have sent to rebel
forces in the Middle East

1355
01:28:56,631 --> 01:28:59,911
nearly $12 million to
overthrow a government

1356
01:28:59,935 --> 01:29:03,881
which you considered nothing
but a religious dictatorship.

1357
01:29:03,905 --> 01:29:05,550
That's absurd.

1358
01:29:05,574 --> 01:29:09,020
Not according to Rahmad Hussein.

1359
01:29:09,044 --> 01:29:12,957
Remember? The man who owns
the clothing store in Beverly Hills.

1360
01:29:12,981 --> 01:29:16,527
He's prepared to
testify that you used

1361
01:29:16,551 --> 01:29:20,131
his contacts in the Middle
East to do exactly that.

1362
01:29:20,155 --> 01:29:22,099
If he wants to perjure
himself, that's his problem.

1363
01:29:22,123 --> 01:29:25,002
Only after awhile when
you realized you were

1364
01:29:25,026 --> 01:29:28,372
supporting a... a
hopeless cause...

1365
01:29:28,396 --> 01:29:30,741
Both in Central America
<i>and</i> the Middle East...

1366
01:29:30,765 --> 01:29:33,578
You decided, "The
hell with them."

1367
01:29:33,602 --> 01:29:35,613
You decided to
call it quits, pull out.

1368
01:29:35,637 --> 01:29:41,085
But this whole guns for
drugs for money operation

1369
01:29:41,109 --> 01:29:42,987
had proved so successful,

1370
01:29:43,011 --> 01:29:44,722
you decided to try
it one more time.

1371
01:29:44,746 --> 01:29:46,457
Only this time,

1372
01:29:46,481 --> 01:29:48,926
you were going to keep all
the money for yourselves.

1373
01:29:48,950 --> 01:29:53,564
But Judge Price was a patriot,
a real patriot, and he refused

1374
01:29:53,588 --> 01:29:55,099
- to go along with you.
- Objection...

1375
01:29:55,123 --> 01:29:58,302
So you had him killed and framed
me for his murder, didn't you?

1376
01:29:58,326 --> 01:30:00,304
I've been patient, but this
whole line of questioning

1377
01:30:00,328 --> 01:30:02,640
is grossly irrelevant
and has now swung

1378
01:30:02,664 --> 01:30:04,842
into bare speculation
and unsupported innuendo.

1379
01:30:04,866 --> 01:30:08,079
Your Honor, the questions
I am asking and must ask,

1380
01:30:08,103 --> 01:30:10,514
are critical to my defense.

1381
01:30:10,538 --> 01:30:11,749
Against my better judgment,

1382
01:30:11,773 --> 01:30:13,284
I'm going to allow
you to continue.

1383
01:30:13,308 --> 01:30:15,253
Objection overruled
without prejudice.

1384
01:30:15,277 --> 01:30:16,687
The People have

1385
01:30:16,711 --> 01:30:19,203
a continuing objection to all
lines of question in this area.

1386
01:30:23,251 --> 01:30:27,965
A couple days ago,
in, uh, that brouhaha

1387
01:30:27,989 --> 01:30:31,502
that your constitutional rights

1388
01:30:31,526 --> 01:30:33,838
keeps you from talking
about, a man was killed.

1389
01:30:33,862 --> 01:30:36,607
A man named Scott Walker.

1390
01:30:36,631 --> 01:30:39,610
Now, he's the man that you hired

1391
01:30:39,634 --> 01:30:43,614
to do all your hands-on
dirty work, isn't he?

1392
01:30:43,638 --> 01:30:45,449
- No.
- Dirty work that finally

1393
01:30:45,473 --> 01:30:47,585
resulted in killing Judge Price.

1394
01:30:47,609 --> 01:30:49,921
- No!
- But when you finally realized

1395
01:30:49,945 --> 01:30:53,424
that he was going to be
arrested and probably coerced

1396
01:30:53,448 --> 01:30:57,028
into telling that you had
hired him to kill Judge Price,

1397
01:30:57,052 --> 01:30:58,362
you killed him.

1398
01:30:58,386 --> 01:31:00,464
I did no such thing.

1399
01:31:00,488 --> 01:31:02,166
Objection, Your Honor.
How far can we let this

1400
01:31:02,190 --> 01:31:04,035
- questioning go?
- A few more moments.

1401
01:31:04,059 --> 01:31:05,425
Overruled.

1402
01:31:08,330 --> 01:31:12,476
Uh, all four of you were issued

1403
01:31:12,500 --> 01:31:17,214
.45 caliber sidearms in
Vietnam, were you not?

1404
01:31:17,238 --> 01:31:19,150
Yes, we were.

1405
01:31:19,174 --> 01:31:20,818
Do you still have yours?

1406
01:31:20,842 --> 01:31:22,987
I did until you subpoenaed it.

1407
01:31:23,011 --> 01:31:25,289
I subpoenaed all
your friends' guns.

1408
01:31:25,313 --> 01:31:29,126
If I told you that
police ballistics

1409
01:31:29,150 --> 01:31:32,797
proved that the gun retrieved

1410
01:31:32,821 --> 01:31:35,533
from Dr. Lehman's office
is the murder weapon,

1411
01:31:35,557 --> 01:31:37,335
would you be surprised?

1412
01:31:37,359 --> 01:31:39,236
Well, I-I'd be...

1413
01:31:39,260 --> 01:31:44,096
disappointed if Gilbert
was involved in a murder.

1414
01:31:45,800 --> 01:31:48,879
But if that's Gilbert's
gun, why am I up here?

1415
01:31:48,903 --> 01:31:51,015
Because it's not his gun.

1416
01:31:51,039 --> 01:31:55,386
His gun was stolen two years
ago... you didn't know that...

1417
01:31:55,410 --> 01:31:58,756
And he went out and
bought another .45.

1418
01:31:58,780 --> 01:32:01,258
And according to the
serial number on file

1419
01:32:01,282 --> 01:32:03,794
at the gun shop where
he bought his new gun,

1420
01:32:03,818 --> 01:32:05,696
this is not his gun.

1421
01:32:05,720 --> 01:32:10,368
His gun... is the
gun you gave us.

1422
01:32:10,392 --> 01:32:13,270
Now, how do you
suppose that happened?

1423
01:32:13,294 --> 01:32:15,840
You switched guns
with him, didn't you?

1424
01:32:15,864 --> 01:32:19,744
You knew the police
would discover that Walker

1425
01:32:19,768 --> 01:32:21,645
had been shot with a .45.

1426
01:32:21,669 --> 01:32:25,483
So, after you shot
him, you hid your gun.

1427
01:32:25,507 --> 01:32:27,952
The next day when you made bail,

1428
01:32:27,976 --> 01:32:29,754
you went back and retrieved it.

1429
01:32:29,778 --> 01:32:34,358
Took it over to
Dr. Lehman's office,

1430
01:32:34,382 --> 01:32:37,261
and unbeknownst to him,
switched guns with him.

1431
01:32:37,285 --> 01:32:43,601
And that's how this gun,
the murder weapon, your gun,

1432
01:32:43,625 --> 01:32:47,071
wound up in
Dr. Lehman's possession

1433
01:32:47,095 --> 01:32:52,410
and your gun, his
gun, wound up in yours.

1434
01:32:52,434 --> 01:32:56,113
That doesn't prove
that I murdered anyone.

1435
01:32:56,137 --> 01:33:03,954
This court is only interested in
whether <i>I</i> murdered someone.

1436
01:33:03,978 --> 01:33:09,560
And I believe what you have
done makes that highly unlikely.

1437
01:33:09,584 --> 01:33:13,297
As for you, Mr. Prescott,

1438
01:33:13,321 --> 01:33:18,869
the City of Los Angeles has
a very fine police department.

1439
01:33:18,893 --> 01:33:22,506
They'll connect you
with Scott Walker.

1440
01:33:22,530 --> 01:33:25,176
They'll prove that you gave him

1441
01:33:25,200 --> 01:33:26,677
the drug that was
administered to me.

1442
01:33:26,701 --> 01:33:32,149
And sooner or later, they'll
prove you killed the man

1443
01:33:32,173 --> 01:33:35,286
you stood beside in the
jungles of Southeast Asia,

1444
01:33:35,310 --> 01:33:38,656
a man on whom you depended,

1445
01:33:38,680 --> 01:33:43,414
a man you called friend.

1446
01:34:08,276 --> 01:34:10,254
Ladies and
gentlemen of the jury,

1447
01:34:10,278 --> 01:34:12,189
have you reached a verdict?

1448
01:34:12,213 --> 01:34:13,704
We have, Your Honor.

1449
01:34:16,551 --> 01:34:19,214
Hope it's a good
day for Geminis.

1450
01:34:21,990 --> 01:34:23,400
What is your verdict?

1451
01:34:23,424 --> 01:34:25,703
We find the
defendant not guilty.

1452
01:34:25,727 --> 01:34:27,872
Thank you ladies and
gentlemen of the jury.

1453
01:34:27,896 --> 01:34:30,541
Mr. Matlock, you stand
acquitted of these charges.

1454
01:34:30,565 --> 01:34:32,610
You're free to go.

1455
01:34:32,634 --> 01:34:34,626
Court is adjourned.

1456
01:34:36,004 --> 01:34:37,982
Yeah. Want a hot dog?

1457
01:34:38,006 --> 01:34:40,985
I'll buy. In Atlanta.

1458
01:34:41,009 --> 01:34:42,653
Wait a minute.

1459
01:34:42,677 --> 01:34:44,788
I wonder if we should
call Mrs. Hawkins

1460
01:34:44,812 --> 01:34:47,158
to see if it's a
good day to travel.

1461
01:34:47,182 --> 01:34:48,844
Oh, the hell with
it. Let's go home.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
